</style><div class="fx-doc" data-doc="partner-agreement" data-version="2026-10-06"><div class="page"><header class="brand"><img class="logo-img" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Fixfy" width="102" height="36"><div class="meta">GETFIXFY LTD, trading as Fixfy · Company No. 15406523 · VAT No. 478 1027 82<br>124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX</div></header><h1 class="title">PARTNER<span class="accent">AGREEMENT</span></h1><p class="version">Version 2026-10-06 · Effective 6 October 2026</p><p>This version replaces version 2026-09-22 for all work offered to you from 6 October 2026. A Booking you accepted before 6 October 2026 stays on the terms that applied when you accepted it.</p><p>THIS AGREEMENT (the “Agreement”) is made on the date it is accepted on the Fixfy platform, between:</p><p>(1) <strong>GETFIXFY LTD</strong>, a company registered in England and Wales under company number 15406523, whose registered office is at 124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX, trading as Fixfy, VAT number 478 1027 82 (“Fixfy”, “we”, “us” or “our”); and</p><p>(2) the independent business, whether a self-employed sole trader, a partnership or a company, whose details are recorded on the Fixfy account that accepts this Agreement (the “Partner”, “you” or “your”). Your legal name, trading name, business address, company number or UTR, VAT number (if you are registered) and bank details are the ones recorded on your Fixfy account.</p><h2 class="section plain">Background</h2><p>Since April 2026 Fixfy has accounted for VAT on its commission only, on the advice of its accountants. This version, effective 6 October 2026, sets out that arrangement in writing.</p><h2 class="section plain">How Fixfy works</h2><p>Fixfy runs a marketplace for home and property services. Customers book Services through Fixfy and independent Partners carry them out. There are two kinds of work, and every Job Offer tells you which one it is.</p><p><strong>Platform Bookings (Schedule A).</strong> A Customer books through Fixfy's website, WhatsApp, telephone or a Fixfy quote. Your contract for the work is with the Customer. Fixfy is your agent: it markets your Services, quotes the Published Price, arranges the Booking and collects the Customer's payment for you. Fixfy keeps a commission, which is a fixed amount per Service set out in the Commission Schedule (or 30% of the price for quoted work that is not in the price list), and pays you the rest. Customer cancellation charges and call-outs are yours in full.</p><p><strong>Fixfy Client Work (Schedule B).</strong> Fixfy has its own contract with a business Client, such as a letting agent, a property manager or a service platform. Fixfy engages you as its subcontractor and pays you a fixed Partner Fee for each Job by self-billing.</p><p>Fixfy does not charge you to join or use the Platform. The only charges Fixfy makes to you are its commission on Platform Bookings and a £50 Late-Withdrawal Fee if you cancel a Booking with 24 hours' notice or less, or do not attend.</p><p>IT IS AGREED as follows:</p><h2 class="section" id="s1"><span class="n">1.</span>Definitions and Interpretation</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c1.1"><span class="n">1.1</span><div class="t">In this Agreement:</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Booking</strong>” means a Job Offer you have accepted, as explained in clause 4. A Booking is either a Platform Booking or Fixfy Client Work.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Client</strong>” means a business with which Fixfy has its own contract to supply Services, such as a letting agent, a property manager, a landlord, a business or a service platform.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Commission</strong>” means the amount Fixfy charges you for its agency services on each Platform Booking: the fixed amount for the Service set out in the Commission Schedule or, for quoted work that is not in the price list, 30% of the quoted price including VAT, unless a different amount is agreed with you in writing before you accept the Booking.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Commission Schedule</strong>” means the schedule of Commission for each Service, attached to this Agreement as an annex and published on the Platform, as updated under clause 8.4.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Customer</strong>” means a person, whether a consumer or a business, who books a Service through Fixfy as a Platform Booking.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Customer Terms</strong>” means Fixfy's booking terms for Customers, published at getfixfy.com/terms, together with Fixfy's 7-day guarantee, as updated from time to time.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Fixfy Channels</strong>” means Fixfy's website, WhatsApp channels, telephone lines and email, and the Platform.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Fixfy Client Work</strong>” means a Job that Fixfy carries out for a Client under Fixfy's own contract with that Client, and engages you to carry out under Schedule B.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Funds Held</strong>” means money Fixfy receives from Customers for Platform Bookings and holds on your behalf until payout, as explained in Schedule A.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement</strong>” means the separate agreement of that name between you and Fixfy, which covers payment collection, receipts and invoices to Customers in your name, Fixfy's VAT invoices to you and self-billing for Fixfy Client Work.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Job</strong>” means a visit or piece of work at a property.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Job Details</strong>” means the information Fixfy gives you on the Platform for each Job: whether it is a Platform Booking or Fixfy Client Work; the Customer's or Client's requirements; the scope of work; the address; the access arrangements; the arrival window; and either, for a Platform Booking, the Published Price, the Commission and your net amount or, for Fixfy Client Work, the Partner Fee.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Job Offer</strong>” means a Job that Fixfy offers or assigns to you through the Platform.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Late-Withdrawal Fee</strong>” means the fee set out in clause 8.3.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Partner Fee</strong>” means the fee Fixfy pays you for Fixfy Client Work, as set out in Schedule B.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Partner Personnel</strong>” means you, if you are an individual, and any individual you supply, engage, employ, contract with or otherwise make available to carry out a Booking on your behalf. References to you carrying out a Booking include Partner Personnel carrying it out.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Payout Statement</strong>” means the statement Fixfy gives you for each payout, as described in clause 9.3.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Platform</strong>” means the Fixfy web platform on desktop, the Fixfy Trade mobile app and email, through which Fixfy offers Jobs to Partners and manages Bookings.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Platform Booking</strong>” means a Job booked by a Customer through the Fixfy Channels, including a quote Fixfy gives on your behalf, that is not Fixfy Client Work and that you carry out under Schedule A.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Published Price</strong>” means the price for a Service that Fixfy publishes or quotes to the Customer on your behalf, inclusive of any VAT, as shown in the Job Details.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Services</strong>” means the services arranged through the Platform, including end of tenancy, deep and after builders cleaning, regular cleaning, painting and decorating, handyman repairs, carpentry, plumbing, electrical work, gardening and property safety certificates.</div></div><div class="cl l2"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">“<strong>Terms of Use</strong>” means the Fixfy Partner Terms of Use as they stand from time to time.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.2"><span class="n">1.2</span><div class="t">Headings do not affect the meaning of this Agreement. “Including” means including without limitation. “In writing” includes email and messages in the Fixfy Trade app.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s2"><span class="n">2.</span>The Platform and the Two Kinds of Work</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c2.1"><span class="n">2.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy runs the Platform. Through it Fixfy receives requests for Services from Customers and Clients at properties they own, occupy or manage, and offers Jobs to independent Partners.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.2"><span class="n">2.2</span><div class="t">On the terms of this Agreement:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.2.1"><span class="n">2.2.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy may from time to time offer Jobs to you, in line with clause 4; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.2.2"><span class="n">2.2.2</span><div class="t">you agree, as an independent business, to carry out the Bookings you accept, yourself or through suitably skilled, experienced and authorised Partner Personnel.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.3"><span class="n">2.3</span><div class="t">Platform Bookings are governed by this Agreement and Schedule A. Fixfy Client Work is governed by this Agreement and Schedule B. If the main body of this Agreement conflicts with a Schedule, the Schedule applies to the work it covers.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.4"><span class="n">2.4</span><div class="t">The Job Details for each Job Offer say whether it is a Platform Booking or Fixfy Client Work. That label decides which Schedule applies. If a Job Offer does not say, ask Fixfy before you accept it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.5"><span class="n">2.5</span><div class="t">By accepting this Agreement you confirm you have received the current Terms of Use and the Commission Schedule. The Terms of Use set out Fixfy's standards and procedures. They are not a contract on their own and Fixfy may change them at any time. Fixfy will tell you about any change by email, in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, and you agree to follow the Terms of Use as they stand at the time of each Job.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s3"><span class="n">3.</span>Your Relationship with Fixfy</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c3.1"><span class="n">3.1</span><div class="t">You are, and remain at all times, an independent business carrying on business on your own account. Nothing in this Agreement makes you or any Partner Personnel an employee or worker of Fixfy, and you must not present yourself or Partner Personnel as such.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.2"><span class="n">3.2</span><div class="t">For Platform Bookings, Fixfy acts as your agent only to the limited extent set out in Schedule A. For Fixfy Client Work, Fixfy is the principal and you are its subcontractor, as set out in Schedule B. Apart from that, nothing in this Agreement creates a partnership, joint venture or agency between you and Fixfy, and you have no authority to make any representation or commitment on Fixfy's behalf.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.3"><span class="n">3.3</span><div class="t">You are fully responsible for, and you will indemnify Fixfy against:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.3.1"><span class="n">3.3.1</span><div class="t">any income tax, corporation tax, National Insurance contributions, PAYE, apprenticeship levy, VAT and any other tax, deduction, contribution, assessment or claim arising from or in connection with the Services carried out by you or Partner Personnel, except where recovery is prohibited by law;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.3.2"><span class="n">3.3.2</span><div class="t">all reasonable costs, expenses and any penalty, fine or interest incurred or payable by Fixfy in connection with any liability under clause 3.3.1; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.3.3"><span class="n">3.3.3</span><div class="t">any liability arising from any employment-related claim, or any claim based on employee, worker, agency worker or similar status, brought against Fixfy by you or any Partner Personnel, and any employer-related liability for breach of immigration requirements relating to Partner Personnel.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.4"><span class="n">3.4</span><div class="t">Each party bears its own expenses in performing this Agreement. You supply your own tools, equipment, products and transport, unless the Job Details say otherwise.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.5"><span class="n">3.5</span><div class="t">This Agreement is not exclusive. You are free to provide services to anyone else and to have an interest in any other business, as long as doing so does not cause you to breach this Agreement or the Terms of Use, including clause 11.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.6"><span class="n">3.6</span><div class="t">It is a material condition of this Agreement that every member of Partner Personnel has, and can evidence, the right to work in the UK at all times, and that you have received and verified their right to work documents. In particular:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.6.1"><span class="n">3.6.1</span><div class="t">before anyone carries out a Booking, you must carry out a right to work check in line with the Home Office guidance in force at the time, and any follow-up checks that guidance requires;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.6.2"><span class="n">3.6.2</span><div class="t">you must follow any instruction Fixfy gives you about immigration law compliance, including a request to audit your compliance, and that of Partner Personnel, with immigration law and right to work checks, and a request to verify the identity of any Partner Personnel;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.6.3"><span class="n">3.6.3</span><div class="t">you must follow any policy or procedure Fixfy introduces on immigration law compliance, including those its Clients require of it;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.6.4"><span class="n">3.6.4</span><div class="t">you must not subcontract a Booking to another business, except by supplying Partner Personnel in line with this Agreement, or with Fixfy's express prior written permission. Where Fixfy gives permission, you must make sure the subcontract contains obligations on the subcontractor equivalent to this clause 3.6, including right to work checks, audit rights and co-operation with the Home Office;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.6.5"><span class="n">3.6.5</span><div class="t">Fixfy may give information about you and Partner Personnel to the Home Office, and to any Client that must check its supply chain, including the structure of the contractual chain through which the Services are provided and the name, legal form, address and registration number of each business in it;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.6.6"><span class="n">3.6.6</span><div class="t">you must co-operate with any Home Office investigation into illegal working and give it any information it asks for;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.6.7"><span class="n">3.6.7</span><div class="t">you must tell Fixfy immediately if you know, or have reasonable cause to suspect, that any Partner Personnel is or may be working illegally; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c3.6.8"><span class="n">3.6.8</span><div class="t">Fixfy may take any step it considers necessary where illegal working is known or suspected, including suspending or ending this Agreement immediately, or requiring that the person does not carry out any Booking. Your own arrangements with Partner Personnel must allow you to take equivalent action.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.7"><span class="n">3.7</span><div class="t">Clause 3.6 is included only for immigration law and right to work compliance. Nothing in it creates or evidences an employment, worker or agency relationship between Fixfy and any Partner Personnel.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s4"><span class="n">4.</span>Job Offers and Bookings</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c4.1"><span class="n">4.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy may offer you Jobs through the Platform: on the Fixfy web platform on desktop, in the Fixfy Trade app, by push notification or by email. You are free to accept or decline any Job Offer. A Job Offer you accept becomes a Booking.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.2"><span class="n">4.2</span><div class="t">If Fixfy assigns a Job to you directly, you may decline it within 24 hours of being notified. If you do not, it becomes a Booking. A Job that starts less than 24 hours after Fixfy notifies you only becomes a Booking once you accept it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.3"><span class="n">4.3</span><div class="t">Each Job Offer shows whether it is a Platform Booking or Fixfy Client Work and:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c4.3.1"><span class="n">4.3.1</span><div class="t">for a Platform Booking, the Published Price, the Commission and your net amount. By accepting it you agree to carry out the work for the Customer at the Published Price; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c4.3.2"><span class="n">4.3.2</span><div class="t">for Fixfy Client Work, the Partner Fee. By accepting it you agree to carry out the work for Fixfy for the Partner Fee.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.4"><span class="n">4.4</span><div class="t">Each Booking forms a separate contract:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c4.4.1"><span class="n">4.4.1</span><div class="t">a Platform Booking forms a contract between you and the Customer, on the Customer Terms and the Job Details, which Fixfy concludes on your behalf as your agent under Schedule A. Between you and Fixfy, it is also governed by this Agreement and the Terms of Use; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c4.4.2"><span class="n">4.4.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy Client Work forms a contract between you and Fixfy, on this Agreement, the Terms of Use and the Job Details. You do not have a contract with the Client.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.5"><span class="n">4.5</span><div class="t">Fixfy is under no obligation to offer you any Job, and you have no right to any Job, including Jobs for Customers, Clients or properties you have worked for before. You are under no obligation to accept any Job.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.6"><span class="n">4.6</span><div class="t">Fixfy may change, reallocate or cancel a Booking if the Customer or Client asks it to or changes its plans, if Fixfy reasonably believes the Booking cannot be carried out safely or to standard, if a document Fixfy needs from you is missing or out of date, or if this Agreement ends. For a Platform Booking, Fixfy does this on your behalf as your agent and in line with the Customer Terms. What you are paid in that case is set out in the Schedules and the Terms of Use.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s5"><span class="n">5.</span>Partner Personnel, Replacements and Cancellations</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c5.1"><span class="n">5.1</span><div class="t">You and Fixfy will tell each other about any absence, cancellation or inability to carry out a Booking in line with the Terms of Use. If you cancel a Booking with 24 hours' notice or less before the arrival window starts, or do not attend, the Late-Withdrawal Fee in clause 8.3 applies, and you authorise Fixfy to arrange for another partner to carry out the work.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.2"><span class="n">5.2</span><div class="t">You are responsible for selecting, engaging, managing, supervising, paying and, where appropriate, replacing Partner Personnel. Subject to clause 5.3, you decide which Partner Personnel carry out each Booking, and you may replace them with other Partner Personnel without Fixfy's approval.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.3"><span class="n">5.3</span><div class="t">Each time you supply someone to carry out a Booking, you warrant that:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c5.3.1"><span class="n">5.3.1</span><div class="t">they are at least 18 years old;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c5.3.2"><span class="n">5.3.2</span><div class="t">they hold a satisfactory Disclosure and Barring Service (“DBS”) check or an equivalent background check;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c5.3.3"><span class="n">5.3.3</span><div class="t">for cleaning, they have at least six months' cleaning experience, and for any other Service, they hold the accreditations and certifications set out in the Terms of Use for that Service;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c5.3.4"><span class="n">5.3.4</span><div class="t">they have the right to work in the UK, checked in line with clause 3.6; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c5.3.5"><span class="n">5.3.5</span><div class="t">as far as you are aware, having made reasonable enquiries, they have not previously been removed from Fixfy for serious misconduct or material breach, and have not behaved while carrying out services in a way that would have justified that.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.4"><span class="n">5.4</span><div class="t">You must make sure that all Partner Personnel are capable of carrying out the Booking and comply with this Agreement, the Terms of Use, the Job Details and the law. You remain fully liable for the acts and omissions of Partner Personnel as if they were your own, and you will indemnify Fixfy against any loss arising from them or from any claim brought by Partner Personnel, including legal fees incurred in defending such claims and any damages or compensation awarded.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.5"><span class="n">5.5</span><div class="t">You are wholly responsible for the pay, benefits, tax, National Insurance, insurance, training, equipment, conduct, health and safety and supervision of Partner Personnel, on whatever terms you agree with them. Fixfy pays you, not Partner Personnel, whoever carries out a Booking.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s6"><span class="n">6.</span>Keys and Access</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c6.1"><span class="n">6.1</span><div class="t">Customers and Clients may give you or Partner Personnel keys, fobs, key safe codes or other means of access to their properties (“Keys”). You are wholly responsible for keeping Keys safe and secure, and you are liable for any loss caused by Keys being lost, stolen, copied or damaged while you or Partner Personnel hold them, including the cost of replacing locks and keys. The rules for Keys are set out in the Terms of Use.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s7"><span class="n">7.</span>Standards, Reports and Photos</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c7.1"><span class="n">7.1</span><div class="t">You will carry out each Booking with reasonable care and skill, in line with the Job Details, the standards in the Terms of Use, good industry practice and the law.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.2"><span class="n">7.2</span><div class="t">You will arrive within the arrival window shown in the Job Details, or at the set time where the Job has one.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.3"><span class="n">7.3</span><div class="t">You will submit the start and completion reports in the Fixfy Trade app, with the photos the app asks for, before you leave the property. The completion report is what makes a Booking ready for payout.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s8"><span class="n">8.</span>What Fixfy Charges You</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c8.1"><span class="n">8.1</span><div class="t"><strong>No joining fee and no plans.</strong> Fixfy does not charge you to join the Platform, to stay on it or to receive Job Offers. Fixfy does not offer paid plans or subscriptions to Partners.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.2"><span class="n">8.2</span><div class="t"><strong>Commission.</strong> For each Platform Booking, Fixfy charges the Commission. For a Service in the price list, the Commission is the fixed amount set out in the Commission Schedule for that Service, unit of time or add-on. For quoted work that is not in the price list, the Commission is 30% of the quoted price, including VAT, unless a different amount is agreed with you in writing before you accept the Booking. The Commission is inclusive of VAT. Fixfy takes no Commission on Customer cancellation charges or call-outs. Fixfy deducts it from the Funds Held for that Booking and issues you a VAT invoice for it with every payout, as set out in the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement. Fixfy does not charge Commission on Fixfy Client Work.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.3"><span class="n">8.3</span><div class="t"><strong>Late-Withdrawal Fee.</strong> If you cancel a Booking of either kind with 24 hours' notice or less before the arrival window starts, or you do not attend, Fixfy charges a Late-Withdrawal Fee of £50 for that Booking. It is Fixfy's charge for finding and arranging a replacement at short notice and for managing the effect on the Customer or Client. It is inclusive of VAT. You agree that it is a reasonable and proportionate charge. Fixfy deducts it from your next payout and shows it on its VAT invoice to you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.4"><span class="n">8.4</span><div class="t"><strong>Changes.</strong> Fixfy may change the Commission Schedule or the Late-Withdrawal Fee by giving you at least 30 days' notice in writing, by email, in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform. Fixfy may change the Partner Fees it offers for future Fixfy Client Work at any time. No change ever affects a Booking you have already accepted.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.5"><span class="n">8.5</span><div class="t">The Commission and the Late-Withdrawal Fee are the only charges Fixfy makes to you. Fixfy may also recover from your payouts the amounts listed in clause 9.5, such as refunds where you are at fault and the cost of remedial work. These are recoveries of money you owe, not charges for Fixfy's services.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s9"><span class="n">9.</span>Payouts</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c9.1"><span class="n">9.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy pays you every two weeks by bank transfer, for the payout periods and on the payout dates set out in the Terms of Use, to the UK bank account in your name recorded on your Fixfy account.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.2"><span class="n">9.2</span><div class="t">Each payout covers:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c9.2.1"><span class="n">9.2.1</span><div class="t">for Platform Bookings, the Funds Held that have become due for payout under Schedule A, less the Commission; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c9.2.2"><span class="n">9.2.2</span><div class="t">for Fixfy Client Work, the Partner Fees for Bookings completed and approved under Schedule B;</div></div><div class="cl l1"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">less any amounts deducted under clause 9.5.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.3"><span class="n">9.3</span><div class="t">For each payout Fixfy gives you a Payout Statement showing, for each Job:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c9.3.1"><span class="n">9.3.1</span><div class="t">for a Platform Booking, the Published Price, any Fixfy promotion paid on the Customer's behalf, the Commission and your net amount; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c9.3.2"><span class="n">9.3.2</span><div class="t">for Fixfy Client Work, the Partner Fee and any materials reimbursed;</div></div><div class="cl l1"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">and, in a separate section, each deduction with its reason. Each Job is always shown at its full value.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.4"><span class="n">9.4</span><div class="t">With each payout Fixfy also issues a VAT invoice for its Commission and any Late-Withdrawal Fee, and a self-bill for any Fixfy Client Work, as set out in the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.5"><span class="n">9.5</span><div class="t">Fixfy may deduct from any payout any amount you owe Fixfy under this Agreement or the Terms of Use, including:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c9.5.1"><span class="n">9.5.1</span><div class="t">the Commission and any Late-Withdrawal Fee;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c9.5.2"><span class="n">9.5.2</span><div class="t">refunds to Customers where you are at fault, and card payments reversed by a Customer's card issuer, under Schedule A;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c9.5.3"><span class="n">9.5.3</span><div class="t">the reasonable cost of remedial work arranged under Schedule A or Schedule B;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c9.5.4"><span class="n">9.5.4</span><div class="t">materials charged back, and the cost of replacing Keys under clause 6; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c9.5.5"><span class="n">9.5.5</span><div class="t">costs under clause 13.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.6"><span class="n">9.6</span><div class="t">If the amount you owe is more than a payout, Fixfy carries the balance forward to the next payout. If no payout is due within 30 days, you will pay the balance within 14 days of Fixfy's written request.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.7"><span class="n">9.7</span><div class="t">If anything on a Payout Statement looks wrong, tell Fixfy within 14 days, as set out in the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.8"><span class="n">9.8</span><div class="t">Any tip a Customer, Client or resident gives for a Booking belongs in full to the Partner Personnel who carried it out. If you pass a tip on through payroll, you bear any tax or National Insurance cost so that the person receives the full amount.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s10"><span class="n">10.</span>Customers, Clients, Complaints and Guarantee</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c10.1"><span class="n">10.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy is the first point of contact for Customers and Clients about any Booking, including complaints. You must pass to Fixfy, through the Platform, any complaint and any request for extra work, a refund or compensation that a Customer, Client or resident raises with you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.2"><span class="n">10.2</span><div class="t">You must give Fixfy the information and help it reasonably asks for about a complaint, within the time set out in the Terms of Use.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.3"><span class="n">10.3</span><div class="t">For Platform Bookings, Fixfy mediates between you and the Customer, and refunds are handled as set out in Schedule A. For Fixfy Client Work, Fixfy decides how to resolve the complaint with the Client, as set out in Schedule B.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.4"><span class="n">10.4</span><div class="t">If work does not meet the Job Details or the standards in the Terms of Use, you will return to put it right at no extra cost, as set out in paragraph A10 of Schedule A or paragraph B6 of Schedule B.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s11"><span class="n">11.</span>Non-Solicitation</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c11.1"><span class="n">11.1</span><div class="t">During this Agreement and for 12 months after it ends, you must not, and you must make sure Partner Personnel do not, directly or indirectly offer or provide services to, or accept payment from, any of the following, other than through Fixfy:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c11.1.1"><span class="n">11.1.1</span><div class="t">any Customer you were introduced to through Fixfy; or</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c11.1.2"><span class="n">11.1.2</span><div class="t">any Client, or any owner, landlord, tenant or resident of a property you attended through Fixfy.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.2"><span class="n">11.2</span><div class="t">Clause 11.1 includes taking payment directly from a Customer for a Platform Booking, for extra work arising from it or for a repeat of it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.3"><span class="n">11.3</span><div class="t">Clause 11.1 does not apply to anyone who was already your customer before you first met them through Fixfy.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.4"><span class="n">11.4</span><div class="t">If you breach clause 11.1, you will compensate Fixfy for the loss it suffers as a result, including the Commission or margin Fixfy would have earned on the work, and Fixfy may end this Agreement immediately. You agree that this restriction is reasonable to protect Fixfy's investment in finding Customers and Clients.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s12"><span class="n">12.</span>Background Checks and Documents</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c12.1"><span class="n">12.1</span><div class="t">You warrant that you are an independent business carrying on business on your own account and that all Partner Personnel have the right to work and to carry out the Services in the UK.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.2"><span class="n">12.2</span><div class="t">You authorise Fixfy and its authorised agents to carry out the checks Fixfy reasonably considers necessary to verify your identity, business status and ability to carry out the Services, including the identity, right to work, DBS status, insurance and qualifications of Partner Personnel under clause 5.3. You agree to give Fixfy the relevant documents for you and all Partner Personnel, and updated documents whenever they change or expire and whenever Fixfy asks. These checks may include credit reference, Basic Disclosure and other background checks.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.3"><span class="n">12.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy keeps your documents on file and may share them with a Client that needs to audit the supply chain for its Jobs, and with a Customer who asks to see evidence of your insurance or accreditation for a Platform Booking.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.4"><span class="n">12.4</span><div class="t">Fixfy may give Customers the information about you that consumer law requires, including your legal name, trading name and business address, as set out in Schedule A.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s13"><span class="n">13.</span>Liability and Insurance</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c13.1"><span class="n">13.1</span><div class="t">You are solely responsible for your work and for any damage, loss or injury to any person or property that happens during or as a result of a Booking, whether caused negligently, recklessly or otherwise.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.2"><span class="n">13.2</span><div class="t">You will indemnify Fixfy against any loss, liability, cost (including reasonable legal costs), damages, charges or expenses Fixfy incurs as a result of a Booking carried out by you or Partner Personnel, including claims by Customers, Clients, residents or third parties, charges or penalties a Client applies to Fixfy, and the cost of remedial work.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.3"><span class="n">13.3</span><div class="t">Throughout this Agreement you must hold public liability insurance of at least £1,000,000 for each claim, covering all the Services you carry out and all Partner Personnel; employers' liability insurance if you employ anyone, as the law requires; and the other insurance set out in the Terms of Use. You must give Fixfy a copy of each certificate when you join and every time it renews. Fixfy's own insurance is for Fixfy's benefit only. It does not cover you or Partner Personnel and does not reduce your liability under this Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.4"><span class="n">13.4</span><div class="t">Fixfy's total liability to you under or in connection with this Agreement is limited to the amounts due to you under it, being the Funds Held due for payout and the Partner Fees for Bookings you have completed and Fixfy has approved. Fixfy is not liable to you for any loss of profit, loss of business or indirect loss.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.5"><span class="n">13.5</span><div class="t">Nothing in this Agreement limits or excludes any party's liability for:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.5.1"><span class="n">13.5.1</span><div class="t">death or personal injury caused by its negligence;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.5.2"><span class="n">13.5.2</span><div class="t">fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation; or</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.5.3"><span class="n">13.5.3</span><div class="t">any other liability that cannot be limited or excluded by law.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s14"><span class="n">14.</span>Termination and Suspension</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c14.1"><span class="n">14.1</span><div class="t">Either party may end this Agreement at any time and for any reason, with immediate effect, by telling the other in writing, by email, in the Fixfy Trade app or by telephone. Otherwise it continues indefinitely.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.2"><span class="n">14.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy may pause the Job Offers it sends you, or remove you from Bookings, while any document Fixfy needs is missing or out of date, while Fixfy looks into a complaint or a quality or safety concern, or if you breach this Agreement or the Terms of Use.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.3"><span class="n">14.3</span><div class="t">When this Agreement ends:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c14.3.1"><span class="n">14.3.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy may reallocate any Booking not yet carried out. For a Platform Booking, you authorise Fixfy to arrange for another partner to carry it out in line with the Customer Terms, and you have no right to the Funds Held for it;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c14.3.2"><span class="n">14.3.2</span><div class="t">you must immediately return any Keys and any property of Fixfy, a Customer or a Client; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c14.3.3"><span class="n">14.3.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy will pay you the Funds Held due for payout and the Partner Fees for Bookings you completed and Fixfy approved before the end, less any amount you owe Fixfy. Fixfy may hold back an amount reasonably needed to cover refunds, guarantee costs and reversed card payments on Platform Bookings completed in the last 14 days, and will pay you the balance once that period has passed.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.4"><span class="n">14.4</span><div class="t">Clauses 3.3, 5.4, 6, 9.5, 9.6, 11, 13, 16.3, 17 and 18, paragraphs A6, A10 and A11 of Schedule A, paragraphs B6, B7 and B8 of Schedule B, sections 16 and 17 of the Terms of Use, and any other provision intended to continue, survive the end of this Agreement.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s15"><span class="n">15.</span>Entire Agreement and Order of Priority</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c15.1"><span class="n">15.1</span><div class="t">This Agreement (including its Schedules and the Commission Schedule), the Terms of Use, the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement and the Job Details of each Booking are the entire agreement between you and Fixfy and replace all earlier agreements and understandings between you and Fixfy, written or oral, on their subject matter. Each party agrees it has no remedy for any statement, representation, assurance or warranty, made innocently or negligently, that is not set out in them. Nothing in this clause limits or excludes liability for fraud, wilful misconduct or deliberate non-disclosure.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c15.2"><span class="n">15.2</span><div class="t">If there is a conflict: this Agreement takes priority over the Terms of Use; the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement takes priority on payment collection, invoicing, self-billing and VAT; and the Job Details take priority over all of them on matters specific to that Booking, such as the scope of work, timing, the Published Price and the Partner Fee.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s16"><span class="n">16.</span>Important Provisions</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c16.1"><span class="n">16.1</span><div class="t">A waiver of any right under this Agreement is only effective if it is in writing, and applies only in the circumstances for which it is given. No delay or failure by Fixfy in exercising any right or remedy operates as a waiver of it, and no single or partial exercise of a right or remedy prevents its further exercise. Rights and remedies under this Agreement are in addition to those provided by law.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.2"><span class="n">16.2</span><div class="t">If any provision, or part of a provision, of this Agreement is invalid, unenforceable or illegal, the rest of the Agreement is not affected. If it would be valid, enforceable and legal with part of it deleted, it applies with the minimum change needed to give effect to the commercial intention of the parties.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.3"><span class="n">16.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy may set off any sum due to you under this Agreement against any sum you owe Fixfy. Unless Fixfy agrees otherwise, you must pay any sum due to Fixfy in full, without any set-off or counterclaim.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.4"><span class="n">16.4</span><div class="t">You may not assign, transfer, charge, subcontract, declare a trust over or deal in any other way with any of your rights or obligations under this Agreement, except that you may supply Partner Personnel to carry out Bookings in line with clauses 3.6.4 and 5. Fixfy may assign, transfer, charge, subcontract or deal in any other way with any of its rights or obligations under this Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.5"><span class="n">16.5</span><div class="t">Fixfy may change this Agreement by giving you at least 14 days' notice by email, in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform. If you accept any Job after the change takes effect, you accept the changed Agreement from that date. If you do not want to accept the changes, your only remedy is to stop accepting Jobs from the date they take effect. Fixfy will keep the current version available on the Platform and keep a record of the date each version took effect.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.6"><span class="n">16.6</span><div class="t">No one other than a party to this Agreement, their successors and permitted assignees has any right to enforce any of its terms. This does not affect any right a Customer has under its own contract with you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.7"><span class="n">16.7</span><div class="t">Notices under this Agreement may be given by email, to the address recorded on your Fixfy account or, for Fixfy, to support@getfixfy.com, or through the Platform.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.8"><span class="n">16.8</span><div class="t">Accepting this Agreement electronically on the Platform, including by signing on screen or tapping to accept, is as binding as signing it by hand. If you accept it for a business, you confirm you are authorised to do so.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s17"><span class="n">17.</span>Data Protection</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c17.1"><span class="n">17.1</span><div class="t">In this Agreement:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.1.1"><span class="n">17.1.1</span><div class="t">“Data Protection Legislation” has the meaning set out in section 3(9) of the Data Protection Act 2018;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.1.2"><span class="n">17.1.2</span><div class="t">“UK GDPR” has the meaning set out in section 3(10) of the Data Protection Act 2018;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.1.3"><span class="n">17.1.3</span><div class="t">“Losses” means losses, damages, liabilities, claims, costs and expenses, including fines, penalties, legal and other professional fees and expenses; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.1.4"><span class="n">17.1.4</span><div class="t">words and expressions defined in Article 4 of the UK GDPR have the same meaning in this Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c17.2"><span class="n">17.2</span><div class="t">Each party will comply with its obligations under Data Protection Legislation in connection with this Agreement. You will comply, and make sure Partner Personnel comply, with Data Protection Legislation and with any data protection, confidentiality and security obligations set out in the Terms of Use or the Job Details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c17.3"><span class="n">17.3</span><div class="t">If and to the extent the parties share personal data in connection with the Services, including the personal data of Customers for Platform Bookings, each party is a separate, and not a joint, controller. A party receiving shared personal data will:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.3.1"><span class="n">17.3.1</span><div class="t">process that personal data only for the purposes of and in connection with the Booking, including any guarantee visit, complaint or payment, and not for any other purpose, including marketing;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.3.2"><span class="n">17.3.2</span><div class="t">promptly tell the other party if it receives any complaint, notice or other communication about the processing of that personal data, or becomes aware of a personal data breach affecting it;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.3.3"><span class="n">17.3.3</span><div class="t">keep that personal data secure with appropriate technical and organisational measures, and delete it once it is no longer needed for the Booking, unless the law requires it to be kept; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.3.4"><span class="n">17.3.4</span><div class="t">make sure the information required under Articles 13 and 14 of the UK GDPR (a privacy notice) is available to any data subject of that personal data.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c17.4"><span class="n">17.4</span><div class="t">You will indemnify Fixfy on demand against all Losses incurred by Fixfy arising from or related to:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.4.1"><span class="n">17.4.1</span><div class="t">your breach of your obligations under this clause 17;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.4.2"><span class="n">17.4.2</span><div class="t">any breach of Data Protection Legislation by you or any Partner Personnel; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c17.4.3"><span class="n">17.4.3</span><div class="t">any claim by a data subject arising from or related to such a breach.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s18"><span class="n">18.</span>Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c18.1"><span class="n">18.1</span><div class="t">This Agreement, and any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with it or its subject matter or formation (including non-contractual disputes or claims), is governed by the law of England and Wales.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c18.2"><span class="n">18.2</span><div class="t">The courts of England and Wales have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any such dispute or claim.</div></div><h1 class="schedule">SCHEDULE A<span class="accent">PLATFORM BOOKINGS</span></h1><p>This Schedule applies to every Platform Booking. Words defined in the Agreement have the same meaning here.</p><h2 class="section" id="sA1"><span class="n">A1.</span>The Contract Is Between You and the Customer</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA1.1"><span class="n">A1.1</span><div class="t">For each Platform Booking, the contract for the Service is between you and the Customer. You supply the Service to the Customer. Fixfy is not a party to that contract and does not supply the Service.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA1.2"><span class="n">A1.2</span><div class="t">That contract is on the Customer Terms and the Job Details. You agree that the Customer Terms apply to every Platform Booking, and you authorise Fixfy to agree them with Customers on your behalf.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA1.3"><span class="n">A1.3</span><div class="t">There are two separate supplies in each Platform Booking:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">your supply of the Service to the Customer, for the Published Price; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">Fixfy's supply of agency services to you, for the Commission. Fixfy's agency services are standard-rated for VAT.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA2"><span class="n">A2.</span>Fixfy's Appointment as Your Agent</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA2.1"><span class="n">A2.1</span><div class="t">You appoint Fixfy as your agent for each Platform Booking, to:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">market your Services to Customers through the Fixfy Channels;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">publish and quote Published Prices for your Services;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">take bookings and conclude them with Customers on your behalf, in line with clause 4 of the Agreement;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">confirm each Booking to the Customer, naming you;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">give Customers, on your behalf, the information the law requires before and after they book;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(f)</span><div class="t">handle cancellations and changes by Customers in line with the Customer Terms;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(g)</span><div class="t">collect payment from Customers as your limited payment collection agent, and issue receipts and invoices to Customers in your name, under the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(h)</span><div class="t">handle first contact with the Customer on complaints, and arrange guarantee visits; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(i)</span><div class="t">make refunds to Customers as this Schedule allows.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA2.2"><span class="n">A2.2</span><div class="t">When Fixfy does these things, it acts in your name and on your behalf. Fixfy does not buy the Service from you and does not resell it to the Customer. Fixfy does not receive or use the Service itself, and it does not change the nature or the value of your supply to the Customer.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA2.3"><span class="n">A2.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy acts only for you in each Platform Booking. It does not act as the Customer's agent.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA2.4"><span class="n">A2.4</span><div class="t">Fixfy's authority is limited to this Schedule. Fixfy cannot commit you to work outside the Job Details or the Customer Terms without your agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA2.5"><span class="n">A2.5</span><div class="t">Fixfy acts as agent for many partners at the same time, including partners who offer the same Services in the same areas. You agree that Fixfy decides which partner to offer each Job to, and that this is not a breach of any duty Fixfy owes you as your agent.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA2.6"><span class="n">A2.6</span><div class="t">A Customer may pay when booking, before any partner has accepted the Booking. Fixfy receives that payment as agent for the partner who accepts the Booking. When you accept, the payment becomes Funds Held for you. If no partner accepts, Fixfy refunds the Customer.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA3"><span class="n">A3.</span>Your Identity and Contact with the Customer</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA3.1"><span class="n">A3.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy names you to the Customer in the Booking confirmation and on the receipt or invoice, using the legal name and trading name recorded on your Fixfy account. Invoicing for a Platform Booking is between you and the Customer: Fixfy issues the receipt or invoice in your name and on your behalf, under the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA3.2"><span class="n">A3.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy may give the Customer the other information about you that consumer law requires, including your business address. Keep the details on your Fixfy account accurate.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA3.3"><span class="n">A3.3</span><div class="t">On site you may give the Customer your name and trading name.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA3.4"><span class="n">A3.4</span><div class="t">During the Booking, including any guarantee visit, contact with the Customer about the Booking runs through the Fixfy Channels: the Fixfy Trade app, Fixfy's WhatsApp and the Fixfy office. This gives the Customer one record and lets Fixfy help if anything goes wrong. Changes, extra work and payment for the Booking are arranged through Fixfy, not directly with the Customer.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA4"><span class="n">A4.</span>Prices, Quotes and Extra Work</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA4.1"><span class="n">A4.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy sets the Published Price for each Service on your behalf, from its price list or from a quote it prepares for the Customer. The Published Price includes any VAT you must charge.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA4.2"><span class="n">A4.2</span><div class="t">By accepting a Platform Booking you agree to carry it out for the Customer at the Published Price shown in the Job Details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA4.3"><span class="n">A4.3</span><div class="t">If extra work or extra time is needed, tell Fixfy through the Fixfy Trade app before you start. Fixfy quotes it to the Customer on your behalf, at the Published Price for that work or at a price you agree with Fixfy, and collects the payment. Do the extra work only once Fixfy confirms that the Customer has agreed. The Commission on extra work is the amount in the Commission Schedule where the work is in the price list or, for quoted work that is not, 30% of the quoted price including VAT, unless a different amount is agreed with you in writing before you accept it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA4.4"><span class="n">A4.4</span><div class="t">Price changes, discounts, refunds and compensation for a Platform Booking are agreed through Fixfy, not directly between you and the Customer.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA5"><span class="n">A5.</span>Materials</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA5.1"><span class="n">A5.1</span><div class="t">You supply the materials included in the Published Price, including cleaning products for cleaning Services and the paint materials pack for painting Services where the Booking includes it. You buy them yourself, and they are part of your supply to the Customer.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA5.2"><span class="n">A5.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy does not sell materials and does not add any markup to materials.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA5.3"><span class="n">A5.3</span><div class="t">If a Job needs materials that are not included in the Published Price, tell Fixfy before you buy them. Fixfy quotes them to the Customer on your behalf at the price you give it, with no Fixfy markup, and collects the payment for you. Fixfy's Commission on extra materials quoted under this paragraph is 30% of their price, including VAT, as set out in the Commission Schedule.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA6"><span class="n">A6.</span>Payment Collection and Funds Held</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA6.1"><span class="n">A6.1</span><div class="t">You appoint Fixfy as your limited payment collection agent for Platform Bookings, on the terms of the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA6.2"><span class="n">A6.2</span><div class="t">When a Customer pays Fixfy for a Platform Booking, that payment discharges the Customer's debt to you for the amount paid, as if the Customer had paid you directly. The Customer has no further liability to you for that amount.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA6.3"><span class="n">A6.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy holds Customer payments for Platform Bookings on your behalf as Funds Held until payout. Fixfy keeps Funds Held readily distinguishable in its records from its own taxable supplies, which are its Commission, its fees and its Fixfy Client Work.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA6.4"><span class="n">A6.4</span><div class="t">Funds Held for a Booking become due for payout when:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">you have completed the Booking and submitted the completion report;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">Fixfy has checked the completion report;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">Fixfy has received the Customer's payment in full; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">there is no open complaint about the Booking.</div></div><div class="cl l1"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">If a complaint is open, Fixfy may hold back the amount in dispute until the complaint is resolved, and pays the rest.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA6.5"><span class="n">A6.5</span><div class="t">Fixfy pays you the Funds Held that are due, less the Commission and any amounts deducted under clause 9.5 of the Agreement, on the next payout date.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA6.6"><span class="n">A6.6</span><div class="t">Fixfy takes reasonable steps to collect what a Customer owes for a Booking, but it does not guarantee payment of an amount the Customer does not pay.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA6.7"><span class="n">A6.7</span><div class="t">Fixfy bears its own payment processing costs. They are never deducted from your net amount.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA6.8"><span class="n">A6.8</span><div class="t">Fixfy keeps Funds Held in a separate account (a dedicated pot of its business bank account) used only for money collected for Partners on Platform Bookings, and records them separately from Fixfy's own money. Funds Held do not earn interest for you.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA7"><span class="n">A7.</span>Commission</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA7.1"><span class="n">A7.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy's income from a Platform Booking is the Commission. Fixfy takes no other margin, markup or fee from the Published Price.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA7.2"><span class="n">A7.2</span><div class="t">For a Service in the price list, the Commission is the fixed amount set out in the Commission Schedule. For quoted work that is not in the price list, it is 30% of the quoted price, including VAT, unless a different amount is agreed with you in writing before you accept the Booking. The Commission is inclusive of VAT at the standard rate. Each Job Offer shows it, and it does not change after you accept the Booking.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA7.3"><span class="n">A7.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy deducts the Commission from the Funds Held at payout and issues you a VAT invoice for it with every payout, even though the Commission is deducted rather than paid by you separately.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA8"><span class="n">A8.</span>Fixfy Promotions</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA8.1"><span class="n">A8.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy may offer Customers discounts, promotional codes or other promotions. Fixfy funds them.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA8.2"><span class="n">A8.2</span><div class="t">Where a Customer uses a Fixfy promotion, Fixfy pays the promotion amount to you as part of the Published Price, on the Customer's behalf. Your price stays the Published Price and your net amount does not change.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA8.3"><span class="n">A8.3</span><div class="t">The receipt shows the Published Price, the promotion amount paid by Fixfy on the Customer's behalf and the amount the Customer paid.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA9"><span class="n">A9.</span>Cancellations</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA9.1"><span class="n">A9.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy handles cancellations and changes by Customers on your behalf, in line with the Customer Terms.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA9.2"><span class="n">A9.2</span><div class="t">Where the Customer Terms charge the Customer a late cancellation charge or a call-out (for example because the Customer cancels late, nobody lets you in or the property is not ready), that charge belongs to you in full. Fixfy collects it on your behalf as Funds Held and pays all of it to you. Fixfy takes no Commission on it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA9.3"><span class="n">A9.3</span><div class="t">To claim a call-out because you could not get in or could not carry out the Booking, wait at least 30 minutes from the start of the arrival window and tell Fixfy through the Fixfy Trade app while you are at the property, with a photo.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA9.4"><span class="n">A9.4</span><div class="t">If the Customer cancels free of charge under the Customer Terms, including under any legal right to cancel, Fixfy refunds the Customer from the Funds Held and nothing is payable to you for that Booking.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA9.5"><span class="n">A9.5</span><div class="t">If you cancel a Platform Booking, or do not attend it, you authorise Fixfy to arrange for another partner to carry it out. Your contract with the Customer for that Booking then ends, and you have no right to the Funds Held for it. The Late-Withdrawal Fee applies if you cancel with 24 hours' notice or less before the arrival window starts, or do not attend.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA10"><span class="n">A10.</span>Guarantee</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA10.1"><span class="n">A10.1</span><div class="t">If the Customer reports, within 7 days of completion (or, for longer-lasting work, within your longer guarantee: painting and decorating 3 months, tiling 3 months, wall treatments 6 months, and woodwork or structural work 6 months), that something in the Job Details was not done or was not done to standard, you will return to put it right at no extra cost. Fixfy arranges the return visit with the Customer, and you will attend within 7 days of Fixfy telling you, at the time Fixfy agrees with the Customer.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA10.2"><span class="n">A10.2</span><div class="t">If you cannot or do not put it right, Fixfy may arrange for another partner to do so and recover the reasonable cost from your Funds Held or later payouts. If that is not possible, Fixfy may refund the Customer, on your behalf, for the part of the work that was not right, from your Funds Held or later payouts. Fixfy will tell you the amount and the reason first.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA11"><span class="n">A11.</span>Complaints, Refunds and Chargebacks</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA11.1"><span class="n">A11.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy handles first contact with the Customer on any complaint and mediates between you and the Customer. You must answer Fixfy's questions within the time set out in the Terms of Use.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA11.2"><span class="n">A11.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy decides fairly, on the evidence, including the Job Details, your reports, photos and messages, whether you are at fault. Fixfy tells you the outcome and the reasons.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA11.3"><span class="n">A11.3</span><div class="t">Where you are at fault, you authorise Fixfy to refund the Customer, in full or in part, from the Funds Held for the Booking or, if they have been paid out, by deduction from later payouts. Where a guarantee visit is a fair remedy, Fixfy will offer it first.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA11.4"><span class="n">A11.4</span><div class="t">Where you are not at fault, any refund or goodwill gesture Fixfy decides to make is funded by Fixfy and does not reduce your net amount.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA11.5"><span class="n">A11.5</span><div class="t">If a Customer's card payment is reversed by the card issuer and the reason is your work, your conduct or your non-attendance, the reversed amount comes from your Funds Held or later payouts. In any other case Fixfy bears it. Fixfy will challenge a reversal where it has reasonable evidence to do so, and your reports and photos are that evidence.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA11.6"><span class="n">A11.6</span><div class="t">If you disagree with a decision under this paragraph, tell Fixfy within 14 days and Fixfy will review it with you in good faith. Nothing in this paragraph affects the Customer's legal rights against you.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA12"><span class="n">A12.</span>Responsibility for the Work</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA12.1"><span class="n">A12.1</span><div class="t">You are responsible to the Customer for the Service, including carrying it out with reasonable care and skill and in line with the law, including the Consumer Rights Act 2015 where the Customer is a consumer.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA12.2"><span class="n">A12.2</span><div class="t">You are responsible for any damage you or Partner Personnel cause, and you hold the insurance set out in clause 13.3 of the Agreement, including public liability insurance of at least £1,000,000 and employers' liability insurance if you employ anyone.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA12.3"><span class="n">A12.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy is responsible to you and to the Customer only for its own agency services.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sA13"><span class="n">A13.</span>VAT and Tax</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cA13.1"><span class="n">A13.1</span><div class="t">The Published Price is the price of your supply to the Customer. The full Published Price, including any promotion paid by Fixfy on the Customer's behalf, counts towards your turnover for VAT and for income tax or corporation tax. You are responsible for monitoring the VAT registration threshold.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA13.2"><span class="n">A13.2</span><div class="t">If you are VAT registered, you account to HMRC for VAT on the full Published Price, and each receipt or invoice Fixfy issues in your name shows your VAT number. The Published Price includes VAT and does not increase because you are registered.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA13.3"><span class="n">A13.3</span><div class="t">If you are not VAT registered, receipts issued in your name show no VAT. You must sign the VAT Status Declaration in the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement and tell Fixfy within 14 days of any change to your VAT status.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA13.4"><span class="n">A13.4</span><div class="t">Fixfy accounts for VAT only on its Commission and its fees.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cA13.5"><span class="n">A13.5</span><div class="t">Fixfy makes no Construction Industry Scheme deductions from Platform Bookings, because Fixfy is not the contractor. It passes on the Customer's payment as your agent.</div></div><h1 class="schedule">SCHEDULE B<span class="accent">FIXFY CLIENT WORK</span></h1><p>This Schedule applies to every Booking of Fixfy Client Work. Words defined in the Agreement have the same meaning here.</p><h2 class="section" id="sB1"><span class="n">B1.</span>Fixfy Is the Principal</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cB1.1"><span class="n">B1.1</span><div class="t">For Fixfy Client Work, Fixfy has its own contract with the Client and is responsible to the Client for the work. Fixfy engages you as its subcontractor to carry out the Job.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB1.2"><span class="n">B1.2</span><div class="t">Each Booking of Fixfy Client Work forms a separate contract between you and Fixfy on the terms of the Agreement, the Terms of Use and the Job Details. You do not have a contract with the Client, but you must follow the Client's requirements and site rules set out in the Job Details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB1.3"><span class="n">B1.3</span><div class="t">The relationship with the Client belongs to Fixfy. You must not agree prices, extra work, refunds or compensation with a Client or resident, or discuss your Partner Fee with them. Pass any such request to Fixfy through the Platform.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sB2"><span class="n">B2.</span>Partner Fee</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cB2.1"><span class="n">B2.1</span><div class="t">For each Booking of Fixfy Client Work, Fixfy pays you the Partner Fee shown in the Job Details when you accepted it. It is a fixed amount for the Job, or a fixed rate per hour, half day or day paid for the time Fixfy approves. The price the Client pays Fixfy is a matter between Fixfy and the Client.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB2.2"><span class="n">B2.2</span><div class="t">A Booking becomes payable once you have completed it, submitted the completion report the Platform asks for, and Fixfy has approved it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB2.3"><span class="n">B2.3</span><div class="t">All Partner Fees are inclusive of any VAT. If you are VAT registered, each self-bill shows the VAT included.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB2.4"><span class="n">B2.4</span><div class="t">Fixfy may change the Partner Fees it offers for future Jobs at any time. A change never affects a Booking you have already accepted.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sB3"><span class="n">B3.</span>Materials</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cB3.1"><span class="n">B3.1</span><div class="t">Fixed-price Jobs include the consumables you normally need for that kind of work. If a Job needs materials that are not included, check with Fixfy through the Platform before you buy them. Fixfy reimburses approved materials at cost when you record them in the completion report with a photo of the receipt.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sB4"><span class="n">B4.</span>How You Attend</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cB4.1"><span class="n">B4.1</span><div class="t">For Fixfy Client Work you attend on Fixfy's behalf, as its independent subcontractor. Follow the Client's rules on identification, conduct and communication set out in the Job Details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB4.2"><span class="n">B4.2</span><div class="t">Do not hand out your own business cards, prices or contact details to the Client or residents, and do not mention any other company or platform to them, except as the Job Details say.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sB5"><span class="n">B5.</span>Cancellations and Changes by Fixfy or the Client</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cB5.1"><span class="n">B5.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy may change, reallocate or cancel a Booking of Fixfy Client Work in the cases in clause 4.6 of the Agreement, and will give you as much notice as it can. Apart from paragraph B5.2, Fixfy is not liable to you for lost fees, Partner Personnel costs or travel costs.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB5.2"><span class="n">B5.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy pays you a call-out of £25, unless the Job Details say a different amount, if:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">the Client cancels the Booking with 24 hours' notice or less; or</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">you cannot carry out the Booking because of the Client, for example because nobody lets you in or the property is not ready, and you tell Fixfy through the Fixfy Trade app while you are at the property, with a photo.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB5.3"><span class="n">B5.3</span><div class="t">You agree the call-out is a genuine pre-estimate of your loss, and you will not claim anything further from Fixfy or the Client for that cancellation.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sB6"><span class="n">B6.</span>Remedial Work</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cB6.1"><span class="n">B6.1</span><div class="t">If the Client reports within 7 days of the Booking that something in the Job Details or checklist was not done, or not done to standard, you will return to put it right at no extra charge, at a time Fixfy agrees with the Client, normally within 48 hours of Fixfy telling you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB6.2"><span class="n">B6.2</span><div class="t">If you cannot or do not, Fixfy may arrange for someone else to do it and deduct the reasonable cost from your payouts.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sB7"><span class="n">B7.</span>Complaints</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cB7.1"><span class="n">B7.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy decides how to resolve any complaint or dispute with the Client, which may include a remedial visit, a repair, a replacement or a refund. Where the cause is your work or the conduct of Partner Personnel, you are responsible for the reasonable cost, including any charge or penalty the Client applies to Fixfy, and Fixfy may deduct it from your payouts after telling you the amount and the reason.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB7.2"><span class="n">B7.2</span><div class="t">If you disagree with a deduction, tell Fixfy within 14 days and Fixfy will review it with you in good faith.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sB8"><span class="n">B8.</span>Self-Billing and CIS</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cB8.1"><span class="n">B8.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy pays you for Fixfy Client Work by self-billing, under the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement. You must not issue your own invoices for Fixfy Client Work.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="cB8.2"><span class="n">B8.2</span><div class="t">Where a Booking of Fixfy Client Work is a construction operation within the Construction Industry Scheme (“CIS”), such as painting and decorating, repairs or building work, and Fixfy is the contractor, Fixfy will verify you with HMRC before paying and make any deduction HMRC requires, at the rate HMRC confirms. The deduction is shown on the self-bill, and Fixfy will give you a CIS payment and deduction statement for each tax month in which a deduction is made.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="sB9"><span class="n">B9.</span>Photos and Reports</h2><div class="cl l1" id="cB9.1"><span class="n">B9.1</span><div class="t">Photos, reports and other material that you or Partner Personnel create for Fixfy Client Work belong to Fixfy, as set out in the Terms of Use.</div></div><div class="execution"><h2>Signed</h2><p>This Agreement has been entered into on the date the Partner accepts it on the Fixfy platform.</p><div class="sigwrap"><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">Getfixfy Ltd</div><div class="script">Victor Braz de Souza</div><div class="sigcap">Signed by Victor Henrique Braz de Souza, Director</div><div class="sigcap">duly authorised, for and on behalf of Getfixfy Ltd</div></div><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">The Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Signature</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Name, duly authorised, for and on behalf of the Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Date</div></div></div><p class="signote">When you sign on screen or tap to accept in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, your acceptance is recorded against this version of the Agreement and binds the Partner (clause 16.8).</p></div><p class="annexnote">Annex: the Commission Schedule, version 2026-10-06 (separate document).</p><footer class="foot"><span>Partner Agreement · Version 2026-10-06</span><span>Getfixfy Ltd, trading as Fixfy · Company No. 15406523 · VAT No. 478 1027 82</span></footer></div></div>$fx$, false
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
  SELECT 1 FROM public.contract_versions WHERE contract_type = 'contractor_service_agreement' AND version = '2026-10-06'
);

INSERT INTO public.contract_versions (contract_type, version, title, body_html, is_active)
SELECT 'terms_of_use', '2026-10-06', 'Partner Terms of Use', $fx$<style>.fx-doc{--navy:#020040;--coral:#ED4B00;--ink:#1c1c2b;--grey:#5d5d6e;--light:#f4f4f8;--line:#dcdce6;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);font-size:10.5pt;line-height:1.55;-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;text-align:left}
.fx-doc *{box-sizing:border-box}
