.fx-doc footer.foot{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:36px;padding-top:8px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;font-size:8.5pt;color:var(--grey)}
.ob-contract .fx-doc .page{max-width:none;margin:0;padding:6px 4px 16px;box-shadow:none}
@media (max-width:640px){.fx-doc .page{padding:24px 16px 32px}.fx-doc header.brand{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}.fx-doc header.brand .meta{text-align:left}.fx-doc h1.title{font-size:20pt}.fx-doc .cl.l2,.fx-doc .cl.sub{margin-left:14px}.fx-doc .cl.l3{margin-left:28px}.fx-doc .cl .n{min-width:34px}.fx-doc .sigwrap{grid-template-columns:1fr}.fx-doc .sigcell + .sigcell{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.fx-doc footer.foot{flex-direction:column}}
@media print{.fx-doc .page{max-width:100%;padding:0 12mm;margin:0;box-shadow:none}.fx-doc .execution{margin-top:20px}.fx-doc footer.foot{margin-top:14px;break-before:avoid;page-break-before:avoid}}
.fx-doc h2.section.plain{margin-top:22px}
.fx-doc h1.schedule{font-size:18pt;color:var(--navy);font-weight:800;margin:40px 0 6px;line-height:1.1;border-top:3px solid var(--coral);padding-top:18px;break-before:page;page-break-before:always}
.fx-doc h1.schedule .accent{color:var(--coral);display:block}
.fx-doc .callout ul{margin:8px 0 0;padding-left:18px}
.fx-doc .callout li{margin:4px 0}
.fx-doc .fieldrow{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-end;margin:10px 0}
.fx-doc .fieldrow .fl{flex:0 0 auto;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy)}
.fx-doc .fieldrow .fv{flex:1 1 auto;border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--navy);height:20px;min-width:80px}
.fx-doc .tick{display:flex;gap:10px;margin:10px 0}
.fx-doc .tick .box{flex:0 0 auto;font-size:14pt;line-height:1;color:var(--navy)}
.fx-doc ol.confirm{margin:8px 0;padding-left:22px}
.fx-doc ol.confirm li{margin:5px 0}
.fx-doc .annexnote{font-style:italic;color:var(--grey)}
</style><div class="fx-doc" data-doc="terms-of-use" data-version="2026-10-06"><div class="page"><header class="brand"><img class="logo-img" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Fixfy" width="102" height="36"><div class="meta">GETFIXFY LTD, trading as Fixfy · Company No. 15406523 · VAT No. 478 1027 82<br>124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX</div></header><h1 class="title">PARTNER<span class="accent">TERMS OF USE</span></h1><p class="subtitle">Fixfy Operating Guide</p><p class="version">Version 2026-10-06 · Effective 6 October 2026</p><p>This version replaces version 2026-09-22 for all work offered to you from 6 October 2026.</p><p>The rules, standards and procedures in these Partner Terms of Use (the “Terms of Use”) apply to every Partner Agreement between GETFIXFY LTD, trading as Fixfy (company number 15406523, registered office 124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX) (“Fixfy”, “we” or “us”), and the independent Partners who use the Fixfy platform. Each of those agreements is the “Partner Agreement”.</p><p>As a Partner, you agree to follow, and to make sure all Partner Personnel follow, these Terms of Use as they stand from time to time. Words defined in the Partner Agreement have the same meaning here. References to you doing something include Partner Personnel doing it.</p><div class="callout"><strong>In short</strong><ul><li>You choose the Jobs you take. We send them through the Fixfy web platform on desktop, the Fixfy Trade app and email.</li><li>There are two kinds of work. <strong>Platform Bookings</strong>: the Customer is your customer, we act as your agent, and you receive the price less Fixfy's commission. <strong>Fixfy Client Work</strong>: the client is ours, and we pay you a fixed Partner Fee by self-billing.</li><li>Every Job Offer shows which kind it is and exactly what you receive.</li><li>We pay every two weeks by bank transfer, with a statement for every Job.</li><li>Joining and using the Platform is free. We have no paid plans.</li><li>Our only charges to you are the commission on Platform Bookings and £50 if you cancel a Booking with 24 hours' notice or less, or don't attend.</li><li>Customer cancellation charges and call-outs on Platform Bookings are yours in full.</li></ul></div><h2 class="section" id="s1"><span class="n">1.</span>About These Terms of Use</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c1.1"><span class="n">1.1</span><div class="t">These Terms of Use support the Partner Agreement. If they conflict, the Partner Agreement takes priority.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.2"><span class="n">1.2</span><div class="t">These Terms of Use are not a contract on their own. Fixfy may change them at any time, as explained in section 20 and clause 2.5 of the Partner Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.3"><span class="n">1.3</span><div class="t">All amounts in these Terms of Use are inclusive of any VAT.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s2"><span class="n">2.</span>Your Account and the Platform</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c2.1"><span class="n">2.1</span><div class="t">Keep your Fixfy account up to date in the Fixfy Trade app, including:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">your legal name, trading name and business address, which Fixfy gives to Customers for Platform Bookings;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">the postcodes and areas you cover, and the days and times you can work;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">the Services you offer and the Partner Personnel who carry them out;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">your documents: insurance, accreditations, right to work and DBS;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">your tax details, including your UTR or company number and your VAT status; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(f)</span><div class="t">your bank details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.2"><span class="n">2.2</span><div class="t">Your login is personal to you. Keep it secure and do not share it. You are responsible for all activity under your account. Tell us straight away if you think someone else has used it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.3"><span class="n">2.3</span><div class="t">Use the Platform only to receive and carry out Bookings. You must not:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">misuse, disrupt, copy, scrape or reverse-engineer the Platform, or try to gain unauthorised access to it or its data;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">give false information, or submit false reports, photos or receipts;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">post, buy or arrange fake reviews or ratings; or</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">hold more than one Fixfy account, unless we agree.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.4"><span class="n">2.4</span><div class="t">We send Job Offers and Booking updates by push notification and email. Keep notifications switched on and your email address and phone number up to date.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.5"><span class="n">2.5</span><div class="t">We may suspend your access if you breach these Terms of Use or the Partner Agreement, or if we reasonably believe your account puts Customers, Clients or the Platform at risk.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s3"><span class="n">3.</span>Job Offers and Bookings</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c3.1"><span class="n">3.1</span><div class="t">We send Job Offers through the Platform: the Fixfy web platform on desktop, the Fixfy Trade app (including push notifications) and email.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.2"><span class="n">3.2</span><div class="t">Every Job Offer is labelled <strong>Platform Booking</strong> or <strong>Fixfy Client Work</strong>, and shows what you receive:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t"><strong>Platform Booking.</strong> The Published Price, the Fixfy commission and your net amount. For example: “Platform Booking · Customer price £223.00 · Fixfy commission £83.00 · You receive £140.00”. The commission for each Service is in the Commission Schedule.</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy Client Work.</strong> The Partner Fee, always labelled in front of the amount: Fixed (a set price for the Job), Hourly (a rate per hour, paid for the hours we approve), Half day or Day rate. For example: “Fixfy Client Work · Fixed · £120.00” or “Fixfy Client Work · Hourly · £40.00/hr”.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.3"><span class="n">3.3</span><div class="t">You may accept or decline any Job Offer. If we assign a Job to you directly, you may decline it within 24 hours of being notified; after that it becomes a Booking. A Job that starts less than 24 hours after we notify you only becomes a Booking once you accept it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.4"><span class="n">3.4</span><div class="t">Some Jobs ask for your price first:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">for a Platform Booking, you quote the price for the Customer, inclusive of any VAT. We show you the commission and your net amount before the quote goes to the Customer. For quoted work that is not in the price list, the commission is 30% of the quoted price, including VAT, unless we agree a different amount with you in writing before you accept. Fixfy sends the quote to the Customer on your behalf, and the Job becomes a Booking only if the Customer accepts it; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">for Fixfy Client Work, your quote is an offer to Fixfy to carry out the work for that amount, and it becomes a Booking only if we confirm it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.5"><span class="n">3.5</span><div class="t">Every day at around 17:00 UK time we email you your Bookings for the next day, in the order you should attend them. Check it, and tell us straight away if anything is wrong.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.6"><span class="n">3.6</span><div class="t">We do not promise any number of Job Offers or Bookings.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s4"><span class="n">4.</span>Fees, Commission and Payouts</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c4.1"><span class="n">4.1</span><div class="t"><strong>Free to join.</strong> Fixfy does not charge you to join the Platform, to stay on it or to receive Job Offers. Fixfy has no paid plans or subscriptions for Partners.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.2"><span class="n">4.2</span><div class="t"><strong>Commission.</strong> On each Platform Booking, Fixfy charges the commission set out in the Commission Schedule, or 30% of the quoted price for quoted work that is not in the price list. The commission is inclusive of VAT. We deduct it from the money we collect for you, and we issue you a VAT invoice for it with every payout. There is no commission on Fixfy Client Work, and none on Customer cancellation charges or call-outs.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.3"><span class="n">4.3</span><div class="t"><strong>Late-Withdrawal Fee.</strong> £50, as set out in section 6.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.4"><span class="n">4.4</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy promotions.</strong> If we give a Customer a discount or a promotion code, we pay that amount to you on the Customer's behalf. Your price and your net amount stay the same.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.5"><span class="n">4.5</span><div class="t"><strong>Payout periods.</strong> We pay in fortnightly periods, each running from a Monday to the second Sunday after it. We pay on the Friday after the period closes. For example, a period that closes on Sunday the 13th is paid on Friday the 18th.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.6"><span class="n">4.6</span><div class="t"><strong>What each payout includes:</strong></div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">Platform Bookings whose money became due for payout by the end of that Sunday: you completed the Booking, submitted the completion report, we checked it, the Customer has paid in full and no complaint is open; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">Fixfy Client Work you completed and we approved by the end of that Sunday.</div></div><div class="cl l1"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">Anything still waiting moves to the payout for the period in which it becomes due.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.7"><span class="n">4.7</span><div class="t"><strong>Money held for you.</strong> Customer payments for Platform Bookings are your money. We hold them on your behalf until payout, and we keep them separate in our records from Fixfy's own income.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.8"><span class="n">4.8</span><div class="t"><strong>Bank account.</strong> We pay into a UK bank account in the Partner's name, as recorded on your Fixfy account. If the Partner is a company, it must be the company's business account. We cannot pay until we have valid bank details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.9"><span class="n">4.9</span><div class="t"><strong>What you receive with each payout:</strong></div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">a Payout Statement showing every Job: for Platform Bookings, the Published Price, any Fixfy promotion paid on the Customer's behalf, the commission and your net amount; for Fixfy Client Work, the Partner Fee and any materials reimbursed; and, in a separate section, any deductions with the reason for each;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">Fixfy's VAT invoice for its commission and any Late-Withdrawal Fee; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">a self-bill for any Fixfy Client Work.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.10"><span class="n">4.10</span><div class="t">If anything looks wrong, tell us within 14 days, as set out in the Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s5"><span class="n">5.</span>Materials</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c5.1"><span class="n">5.1</span><div class="t"><strong>Platform Bookings.</strong> You supply the materials included in the Published Price, including cleaning products for cleaning Services and the paint and materials pack for painting Services when the Customer adds it. Fixfy does not sell materials or add a markup to them. If a Job needs materials that are not included, tell us through the Fixfy Trade app before you buy them. We quote them to the Customer on your behalf at the price you give us and collect the payment for you, with no Fixfy markup. Fixfy's commission on extra materials is 30% of their price, including VAT, as set out in the Commission Schedule.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.2"><span class="n">5.2</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy Client Work.</strong> Fixed-price Jobs include the consumables you normally need for that kind of work. If a Job needs materials that are not included, check with us through the Platform before you buy them. We reimburse approved materials at cost when you record them in the completion report with a photo of the receipt.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s6"><span class="n">6.</span>Cancellations and Absences by You</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c6.1"><span class="n">6.1</span><div class="t">Once you have accepted a Booking, you may cancel it, or tell us you cannot supply Partner Personnel for it, free of charge if you give us more than 24 hours' notice before the arrival window starts. Cancel in the Fixfy Trade app or by contacting the Fixfy office.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.2"><span class="n">6.2</span><div class="t">If you cancel with 24 hours' notice or less, or you do not attend, Fixfy charges a Late-Withdrawal Fee of £50 for each Booking. It is Fixfy's charge for finding a replacement at short notice and managing the effect on the Customer or Client. It is inclusive of VAT, deducted from your next payout and shown on Fixfy's VAT invoice to you.</div></div><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th>When you tell us</th><th>Late-Withdrawal Fee</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>More than 24 hours before the arrival window starts</td><td>£0</td></tr><tr><td>24 hours or less before the arrival window starts</td><td>£50</td></tr><tr><td>You do not attend, or you do not tell us at all</td><td>£50</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="cl l1" id="c6.3"><span class="n">6.3</span><div class="t">The Late-Withdrawal Fee does not cover property or materials lost, damaged or wasted as a result of your cancellation, which you still owe.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.4"><span class="n">6.4</span><div class="t">You are not paid for any part of a Booking you do not carry out. For a Platform Booking, we arrange another partner for the Customer on your behalf, your contract with the Customer for that Booking ends, and the money for it goes to the partner who does the work.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.5"><span class="n">6.5</span><div class="t">If you are going to arrive after the start of the arrival window, tell us through the app as soon as you know, and in any case before the window starts. If you arrive after the window ends without having told us, we may treat the Booking as one you did not attend.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.6"><span class="n">6.6</span><div class="t">Give us at least one week's notice if you will not be able to carry out Bookings you have accepted because of a holiday, business closure, staffing or any other planned reason.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.7"><span class="n">6.7</span><div class="t">Repeated late cancellations or missed Bookings may lead us to offer you fewer Jobs, pause your account or end the Partner Agreement.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s7"><span class="n">7.</span>Cancellations and Changes by Customers, Clients or Fixfy</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c7.1"><span class="n">7.1</span><div class="t">We may change, reallocate or cancel a Booking in the cases in clause 4.6 of the Partner Agreement. We give you as much notice as we can.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.2"><span class="n">7.2</span><div class="t"><strong>Platform Bookings.</strong> We handle Customer cancellations and changes on your behalf, under the Customer Terms. Where the Customer Terms charge the Customer a late cancellation charge or a call-out, that charge is yours in full: we collect it for you and pay all of it to you, with no commission. At the date of these Terms of Use, the Customer Terms set this charge at 50% of the price of the services cancelled when the Customer cancels less than 48 hours before the arrival window starts, or when you cannot get in. If the Customer cancels free of charge under the Customer Terms or the law, we refund the Customer and nothing is payable to you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.3"><span class="n">7.3</span><div class="t"><strong>If you cannot get in.</strong> Wait at least 30 minutes from the start of the arrival window, try the access arrangements in the Job Details and tell us through the app while you are at the property, with a photo. We then try to reach the Customer or Client. If nobody lets you in, the call-out in section 7.2 or 7.4 applies.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.4"><span class="n">7.4</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy Client Work.</strong> We pay you a call-out of £25, unless the Job Details say a different amount, if:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">the Client cancels the Booking with 24 hours' notice or less; or</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">you cannot carry out the Booking because of the Client, for example because nobody lets you in or the property is not ready, and you tell us as set out in section 7.3.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.5"><span class="n">7.5</span><div class="t">Apart from sections 7.2 and 7.4, we are not liable to you for lost fees, Partner Personnel costs or travel costs. You agree the call-out is a genuine pre-estimate of your loss, and you will not claim anything further from Fixfy, the Customer or the Client for that cancellation.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s8"><span class="n">8.</span>Partner Personnel and Accreditations</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c8.1"><span class="n">8.1</span><div class="t">You are responsible for selecting, engaging, managing, supervising, paying and, where appropriate, replacing the Partner Personnel who carry out Bookings. You decide who carries out each Booking and may replace them without our approval, as long as the replacement meets section 8.2.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.2"><span class="n">8.2</span><div class="t">Before anyone carries out a Booking, you must make sure that:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">they are at least 18 years old;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">they hold a satisfactory DBS check (at least a basic DBS) or an equivalent background check;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">for cleaning, they have at least six months' cleaning experience;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">for any other Service, they hold the accreditations in section 8.5; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">their right to work has been checked in line with section 19.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.3"><span class="n">8.3</span><div class="t">Before someone attends a Booking for the first time, tell us their name through the app or by email, so we can tell the Customer or Client who is coming, and keep their right to work and DBS evidence ready to give us.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.4"><span class="n">8.4</span><div class="t">You are wholly responsible for paying, training, equipping, insuring, supervising and managing Partner Personnel. Fixfy pays you under the normal arrangements, and never pays Partner Personnel directly.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.5"><span class="n">8.5</span><div class="t"><strong>Minimum accreditations.</strong> These are the minimum for each Service. You also warrant that you hold any other certification, accreditation, insurance and training required by law or by good industry practice. Certificates are issued by you, in your own name and registration.</div></div><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Minimum accreditation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cleaning (end of tenancy, deep, after builders, regular)</td><td>At least six months' cleaning experience</td></tr><tr><td>Handyman repairs, carpentry, painting and decorating</td><td>Asbestos awareness training (Control of Asbestos Regulations 2012, regulation 10)</td></tr><tr><td>Plumbing</td><td>NVQ Level 2 or 3 in Plumbing; G3 unvented hot water certification where the Job involves unvented systems</td></tr><tr><td>Electrical work and Electrical Installation Condition Reports (EICR)</td><td>Membership of a Competent Person Scheme (NICEIC, NAPIT, ELECSA or Stroma)</td></tr><tr><td>Gas work, boiler services and gas safety certificates</td><td>Gas Safe registration for the work carried out (CCN1 and CENWAT as a minimum); G3 where relevant</td></tr><tr><td>Appliance repair</td><td>City &amp; Guilds NVQ Level 3 in domestic appliance servicing; Gas Safe and F-Gas certification where the Job involves them</td></tr><tr><td>Energy Performance Certificates (EPC)</td><td>Accredited Domestic Energy Assessor with a government-approved accreditation scheme</td></tr><tr><td>PAT testing</td><td>Qualified and competent to test portable appliances (for example City &amp; Guilds 2377)</td></tr><tr><td>Fire risk assessments</td><td>Competent assessor with a recognised fire risk assessment qualification or registration</td></tr><tr><td>Fire alarms, emergency lighting and extinguishers</td><td>Competent engineer working to BS 5839, BS 5266 or BS 5306 as relevant</td></tr><tr><td>Gardening and waste removal</td><td>Waste carrier registration if you take any waste away</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 class="section" id="s9"><span class="n">9.</span>Carrying Out the Job</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c9.1"><span class="n">9.1</span><div class="t"><strong>Arrival.</strong> Arrive within the arrival window shown in the Job Details, or at the set time where the Job has one.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.2"><span class="n">9.2</span><div class="t"><strong>Scope.</strong> Carry out the work in the Job Details, following our checklists (such as the end of tenancy checklist) and the Customer's or Client's requirements. Do extra work only once it has been approved through the Platform before you start. For a Platform Booking, that means we have confirmed the Customer agreed to it and to its price. You are not paid for work that has not been approved.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.3"><span class="n">9.3</span><div class="t"><strong>Reports and photos.</strong> Submit the start and completion reports in the Fixfy Trade app, with the photos the app asks for, before you leave the property. The completion report is what makes a Booking ready for payout, and it is your evidence if a Customer complains or disputes a payment. Photos must show the property and the work only: never people, documents, post or anything else that identifies the resident.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.4"><span class="n">9.4</span><div class="t"><strong>Problems on site.</strong> If you find damage, a safety issue, an access problem or work that is not in the scope, stop and tell us through the app straight away, with photos. You may stop work if the property is unsafe; we explain why to the Customer or Client and agree the next step.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.5"><span class="n">9.5</span><div class="t"><strong>Guarantee and remedial visits.</strong></div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t"><strong>Platform Bookings.</strong> Every Platform Booking carries your guarantee to the Customer: 7 days as standard, and for longer-lasting work painting and decorating 3 months, tiling 3 months, wall treatments 6 months, and woodwork or structural work 6 months. If the Customer reports within that period that something was not done, or not done to standard, you return to put it right at no extra cost. We arrange the visit with the Customer, and you attend within 7 days of us telling you. For an end of tenancy clean this includes the free re-clean when the letting agent or landlord flags an item on the Fixfy checklist. For a certificate, it includes correcting and reissuing the certificate if it contains a mistake.</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy Client Work.</strong> If the Client reports within 7 days of the Booking that something in the Job Details or checklist was not done, or not done to standard, you return to put it right at no extra charge, at a time we agree with the Client, normally within 48 hours of us telling you.</div></div><div class="cl l1"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">If you cannot return, paragraph A10 or B6 of the Partner Agreement applies.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.6"><span class="n">9.6</span><div class="t"><strong>Waste.</strong> Only take waste away from a property if the Job includes it and you hold a waste carrier registration, and always dispose of it lawfully.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s10"><span class="n">10.</span>Conduct and How You Present Yourself</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c10.1"><span class="n">10.1</span><div class="t"><strong>On every Booking.</strong> Be courteous, punctual and tidy. Do not smoke, vape or drink alcohol at the property. Do not bring anyone who is not carrying out the Booking. Respect the privacy of residents and their belongings.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.2"><span class="n">10.2</span><div class="t"><strong>Platform Bookings.</strong> You attend as your own independent business, on a Booking Fixfy arranged as your agent. You may give the Customer your name and trading name. During the Booking, including any guarantee visit, contact with the Customer about the Booking runs through Fixfy's channels: the Fixfy Trade app, Fixfy's WhatsApp and the Fixfy office. That gives the Customer one record and lets us help if anything goes wrong. Changes, extra work and payment are arranged through Fixfy, and you must not take payment directly from the Customer.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.3"><span class="n">10.3</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy Client Work.</strong> You attend on Fixfy's behalf, as its independent subcontractor. Follow the Client's rules set out in the Job Details. Do not hand out your own business cards, prices or contact details to the Client or residents, and do not mention any other company or platform to them, except as the Job Details say.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.4"><span class="n">10.4</span><div class="t">Clause 11 of the Partner Agreement (non-solicitation) applies to both kinds of work.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s11"><span class="n">11.</span>Keys and Access</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c11.1"><span class="n">11.1</span><div class="t">When you receive Keys, you must:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">tell us straight away that you are holding them;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">tag them with the unique code we give you; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">make sure the Customer's or Client's name, address and other identifying details are never written on or near them.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.2"><span class="n">11.2</span><div class="t">Unless we authorise it in writing, you must not give or lend Keys to anyone other than the Partner Personnel carrying out the Booking, and you must not copy them. Never share or write down key safe or access codes.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.3"><span class="n">11.3</span><div class="t">Tell us immediately if any Keys held by you or Partner Personnel are lost, stolen or damaged.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.4"><span class="n">11.4</span><div class="t">Whenever we, the Customer or the Client ask, hand over all Keys immediately to Fixfy, the Customer, the Client or whoever we tell you, at your own cost.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.5"><span class="n">11.5</span><div class="t">If you do not follow this section, we may withhold any payout due to you until you do.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s12"><span class="n">12.</span>Equipment and Supplies</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c12.1"><span class="n">12.1</span><div class="t">You provide your own tools, equipment and products, unless the Job Details say otherwise. Do not use the Customer's or Client's own supplies unless the Job Details say you may.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.2"><span class="n">12.2</span><div class="t">Everything you use must be fit for purpose and safe, and used in line with the manufacturer's instructions, normal industry practice and the rules on hazardous substances (COSHH).</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s13"><span class="n">13.</span>Quality, Ratings and Reviews</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c13.1"><span class="n">13.1</span><div class="t">We track quality on every Booking, including Customer and Client feedback and ratings, report completeness, punctuality, cancellations and complaints. You agree to carry out the Services professionally and in a way that seeks the best possible feedback.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.2"><span class="n">13.2</span><div class="t">Customers may rate and review your work. We may publish ratings and reviews of Platform Bookings on the Platform and on getfixfy.com, under your trading name.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.3"><span class="n">13.3</span><div class="t">Customer and Client ratings and feedback are outside our control, and we are not liable for any loss you suffer because of them.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.4"><span class="n">13.4</span><div class="t">If your quality, reliability or complaint record falls below our standards, we may offer you fewer Jobs, pause your account or end the Partner Agreement.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s14"><span class="n">14.</span>Insurance</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c14.1"><span class="n">14.1</span><div class="t">Throughout the Partner Agreement you must hold:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">public liability insurance of at least £1,000,000 for each claim, covering all the Services you carry out and all Partner Personnel;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">employers' liability insurance if you employ anyone, as the law requires (at least £5,000,000); and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">any other insurance the law requires for your Services, and professional indemnity insurance where you issue certificates or reports (for example EICR, gas safety, EPC or fire risk assessments).</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.2"><span class="n">14.2</span><div class="t">Upload your insurance certificates to your Fixfy account when you join and every time they renew. We may pause Job Offers while a certificate is missing or out of date.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.3"><span class="n">14.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy's own insurance is maintained for Fixfy's benefit only. You are not a named insured under it and it does not cover you or Partner Personnel for the Services.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.4"><span class="n">14.4</span><div class="t">If you become aware of anything that could lead to a claim, tell us without delay, and give us and our insurers the information, help and signed documents we reasonably ask for.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s15"><span class="n">15.</span>Damage, Complaints, Refunds and Disputes</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c15.1"><span class="n">15.1</span><div class="t">If anything is broken or damaged during a Booking, you must tell us through the app as soon as possible, with photos and details; not agree anything with the Customer, Client or resident yourself; and answer our questions within 48 hours.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c15.2"><span class="n">15.2</span><div class="t"><strong>Platform Bookings.</strong> We are the Customer's first point of contact and we mediate between you and the Customer. We decide fairly, on the evidence, whether you are at fault, and tell you the outcome and the reasons. Where you are at fault, we offer a guarantee visit first where that is a fair remedy, and any refund to the Customer comes from the money we hold for you for that Booking or from later payouts. Where you are not at fault, any goodwill gesture we choose to make is paid by Fixfy. If a Customer's card payment is reversed because of your work, conduct or non-attendance, the reversed amount comes from the money we hold for you or later payouts; otherwise Fixfy bears it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c15.3"><span class="n">15.3</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy Client Work.</strong> We decide how to resolve any complaint or dispute with the Client, which may include a remedial visit, a repair, a replacement or a refund. Where the cause is your work or the conduct of Partner Personnel, you are responsible for the reasonable cost, and we may deduct it from your payouts after telling you the amount and the reason.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c15.4"><span class="n">15.4</span><div class="t">If you disagree with a decision or a deduction, tell us within 14 days and we will review it with you in good faith.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s16"><span class="n">16.</span>Intellectual Property and Photos</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c16.1"><span class="n">16.1</span><div class="t">“Intellectual Property Rights” means patents, copyright and related rights, trade marks, business and domain names, goodwill and the right to sue for passing off, rights in designs, software and databases, rights in confidential information and know-how, and all similar rights anywhere in the world, whether registered or not.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.2"><span class="n">16.2</span><div class="t">All Intellectual Property Rights in Fixfy's business, including the Fixfy name and logo and the Platform, belong to Fixfy. You may tell a Customer that a Booking was arranged through Fixfy. Otherwise you may not use them for any purpose without our written permission, during or after the Partner Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.3"><span class="n">16.3</span><div class="t">You may not use the name, logo or brand of any Client for any purpose.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.4"><span class="n">16.4</span><div class="t"><strong>Platform Bookings.</strong> You keep ownership of the photos, reports and other material that you or Partner Personnel create for a Platform Booking. You grant Fixfy, and will make sure Partner Personnel grant Fixfy, a non-exclusive, perpetual, royalty-free licence to use, copy, store and share them to evidence the work to the Customer, to handle complaints, guarantee visits and payment disputes, and, with personal details removed, in Fixfy's own materials.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c16.5"><span class="n">16.5</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy Client Work.</strong> Photos, reports and other material that you or Partner Personnel create for Fixfy Client Work belong to Fixfy. You assign, and will make sure Partner Personnel assign, all rights in them to Fixfy, and waive any moral rights in them. We may use them to evidence the work to Clients and, with personal details removed, in our own materials. You may not use them for any other purpose.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s17"><span class="n">17.</span>Confidential Information</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c17.1"><span class="n">17.1</span><div class="t">“Confidential Information” means any information, in any form, about the business, Customers, Clients, residents, properties, prices, systems, affairs or finances of Fixfy or of any Client, including information you create, receive or obtain in connection with the Partner Agreement, whether or not it is marked confidential.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c17.2"><span class="n">17.2</span><div class="t">You will not, and will make sure Partner Personnel do not, use or disclose Confidential Information to anyone, except to carry out Bookings, either during the Partner Agreement or at any time after it ends. You will use your best endeavours to prevent its publication or disclosure.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c17.3"><span class="n">17.3</span><div class="t">These restrictions do not apply to any use or disclosure authorised by Fixfy or required by law, or to information that is or becomes public other than through your breach.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c17.4"><span class="n">17.4</span><div class="t">If a Client asks, you will, and will make sure Partner Personnel will, sign a separate confidentiality agreement for that Client's Jobs.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c17.5"><span class="n">17.5</span><div class="t">Nothing in the Partner Agreement or these Terms of Use prevents you or Partner Personnel from making a protected disclosure, co-operating with or giving information to any regulatory, supervisory, investigatory or prosecuting body, reporting an offence to the police, reporting anything the law requires you to report, or discussing these matters with professional advisers or medical professionals who owe a duty of confidentiality.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s18"><span class="n">18.</span>Data Protection</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c18.1"><span class="n">18.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy holds and processes data about you and Partner Personnel for legal, contractual and legitimate business purposes, including: identity, contact, business, tax and bank details; right to work, DBS, insurance and accreditation documents; and activity on the Platform, such as Job acceptances, check-in times, reports and photos. Where needed, this includes special category and criminal records data, for example DBS results needed to meet legal and Client requirements, and right to work documents that may reveal nationality.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c18.2"><span class="n">18.2</span><div class="t">You will, and will make sure Partner Personnel will, comply with Data Protection Legislation and with our data protection policy when handling personal data of Customers, Clients, residents or anyone else in connection with a Booking. Use Customer and resident details only to carry out the Booking, including any guarantee visit, and never for marketing. Delete them once you no longer need them.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c18.3"><span class="n">18.3</span><div class="t">We share with Customers your legal name, trading name and business address, and your VAT number if you are registered, as consumer law and VAT rules require. We may also share with Customers and Clients the name and, where they ask, the photo of the Partner Personnel attending, and your business details where a Client needs to check its supply chain.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c18.4"><span class="n">18.4</span><div class="t">Our privacy notice for Partners explains how we use personal data. You can ask for it at any time at support@getfixfy.com.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s19"><span class="n">19.</span>Right to Work Checks</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c19.1"><span class="n">19.1</span><div class="t">Before anyone carries out a Booking, you must check their right to work in line with the Home Office guidance in force at the time, including any follow-up check, and make sure nobody starts a Booking before that check has been completed.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c19.2"><span class="n">19.2</span><div class="t">You must tell us immediately about any change in the immigration status or personal circumstances of any Partner Personnel that may affect their right to work in the UK.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c19.3"><span class="n">19.3</span><div class="t">We may take any step we consider necessary for right to work compliance, including cancelling or stopping a Booking immediately where we reasonably believe the person attending does not have the right to work in the UK.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c19.4"><span class="n">19.4</span><div class="t">You must comply with any request from us to audit your compliance, and that of Partner Personnel, with immigration law and right to work checks, including any request to verify the identity of Partner Personnel, and you must co-operate with any Home Office investigation into illegal working.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c19.5"><span class="n">19.5</span><div class="t">When we ask, you must give us written confirmation that the prescribed right to work checks have been carried out on all Partner Personnel who carry out, or are due to carry out, Bookings, with the date of each check and, where relevant, when the follow-up check is due. Keep copies of all right to work documents and give them to us promptly when we ask, for any audit or Home Office investigation.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s20"><span class="n">20.</span>Changes to These Terms of Use</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c20.1"><span class="n">20.1</span><div class="t">We may change these Terms of Use at any time. We tell you about any change by email, in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, and keep the current version available on the Platform.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c20.2"><span class="n">20.2</span><div class="t">A change applies to Jobs offered after it takes effect. It never changes the Published Price, commission or Partner Fee of a Booking you have already accepted. Changes to the Commission Schedule and the Late-Withdrawal Fee need 30 days' notice, as set out in clause 8.4 of the Partner Agreement.</div></div><div class="execution"><h2>Signed</h2><p>By signing or accepting in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, the Partner confirms it has read these Terms of Use and agrees to follow them, and to make sure all Partner Personnel follow them.</p><div class="sigwrap"><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">Issued by Getfixfy Ltd</div><div class="script">Victor Braz de Souza</div><div class="sigcap">Signed by Victor Henrique Braz de Souza, Director</div><div class="sigcap">duly authorised, for and on behalf of Getfixfy Ltd</div></div><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">Accepted by the Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Signature</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Name, duly authorised, for and on behalf of the Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Date</div></div></div><p class="signote">Your acceptance is recorded on the Platform against this version of the Terms of Use.</p></div><footer class="foot"><span>Partner Terms of Use · Version 2026-10-06</span><span>Getfixfy Ltd, trading as Fixfy · Company No. 15406523 · VAT No. 478 1027 82</span></footer></div></div>$fx$, false
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
  SELECT 1 FROM public.contract_versions WHERE contract_type = 'terms_of_use' AND version = '2026-10-06'
);

INSERT INTO public.contract_versions (contract_type, version, title, body_html, is_active)
