</style><div class="fx-doc" data-doc="invoicing-and-payment-collection" data-version="2026-10-06"><div class="page"><header class="brand"><img class="logo-img" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Fixfy" width="102" height="36"><div class="meta">GETFIXFY LTD, trading as Fixfy · Company No. 15406523 · VAT No. 478 1027 82<br>124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX</div></header><h1 class="title">INVOICING AND PAYMENT<span class="accent">COLLECTION AGREEMENT</span></h1><p class="version">Version 2026-10-06 · Effective 6 October 2026</p><p>This agreement replaces the Self-Billing Agreement version 2026-09-22 for all work offered to the Partner from 6 October 2026.</p><p>This Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement (the “Agreement”) is made on the date it is accepted on the Fixfy platform, between:</p><p>(1) <strong>GETFIXFY LTD</strong>, a company registered in England and Wales under company number 15406523, whose registered office is at 124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX, trading as Fixfy, VAT number 478 1027 82 (“Fixfy”, “we” or “us”); and</p><p>(2) the independent business whose details are recorded on the Fixfy account that accepts this Agreement (the “Partner”, “you” or “your”). Your legal name, trading name, business address, company number or UTR and VAT registration number (if you are registered) are the ones recorded on that account and in your VAT Status Declaration.</p><p>It applies to the work you carry out under the Fixfy Partner Agreement. Words defined in the Partner Agreement and the Partner Terms of Use have the same meaning here.</p><h2 class="section plain">Background</h2><p>Since April 2026 Fixfy has accounted for VAT on its commission only, on the advice of its accountants. This version, effective 6 October 2026, sets out that arrangement in writing.</p><div class="callout"><strong>What this agreement does</strong><ul><li><strong>Platform Bookings.</strong> The Customer is your customer. Fixfy collects the Customer's payment for you, issues the receipt or invoice to the Customer in your name, holds the money for you and pays it to you less Fixfy's commission. Fixfy gives you a VAT invoice for its commission with every payout.</li><li><strong>Fixfy Client Work.</strong> Fixfy is your customer. Fixfy prepares your invoice for you (self-billing) and pays it.</li><li>You don't need to send invoices to Fixfy or to Customers, and you must not send your own invoice for the same work.</li><li>You tell Fixfy your VAT status once, in the VAT Status Declaration in Annex 1, and you tell Fixfy within 14 days if it changes.</li></ul></div><h2 class="section" id="s1"><span class="n">1.</span>Scope</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c1.1"><span class="n">1.1</span><div class="t">Sections 2 to 6 apply to Platform Bookings (Schedule A of the Partner Agreement).</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.2"><span class="n">1.2</span><div class="t">Section 7 applies to Fixfy Client Work (Schedule B of the Partner Agreement) only.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.3"><span class="n">1.3</span><div class="t">Sections 8 to 14 and Annex 1 apply to both.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s2"><span class="n">2.</span>Fixfy's Appointment as Your Limited Payment Collection Agent</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c2.1"><span class="n">2.1</span><div class="t">For each Platform Booking, you appoint Fixfy as your limited payment collection agent, to receive payment from the Customer on your behalf by card through Fixfy's payment provider, by bank transfer or by any other method Fixfy offers Customers.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.2"><span class="n">2.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy's appointment is limited to:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">receiving Customer payments for Platform Bookings, including deposits, balances, extra work, extra materials, cancellation charges and call-outs under the Customer Terms;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">holding them on your behalf as Funds Held;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">making refunds to Customers as the Partner Agreement allows;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">deducting the Commission and the other amounts set out in section 9; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">paying the balance to you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.3"><span class="n">2.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy acts only for you in collecting payment. It does not act as the Customer's agent.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.4"><span class="n">2.4</span><div class="t">A payment a Customer makes to Fixfy for a Platform Booking discharges the Customer's debt to you for that amount, as if the Customer had paid you directly. The Customer has no further liability to you for it, and you must not ask the Customer to pay you again for any amount the Customer has paid Fixfy.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.5"><span class="n">2.5</span><div class="t">A Customer may pay when booking, before any partner has accepted the Booking. Fixfy receives that payment as agent for the partner who accepts the Booking. When you accept, it becomes Funds Held for you. If no partner accepts, Fixfy refunds the Customer.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.6"><span class="n">2.6</span><div class="t">Fixfy takes reasonable steps to collect what a Customer owes for a Booking, including sending payment links and reminders. Fixfy is not obliged to take legal action and does not guarantee payment. If a Customer does not pay, Fixfy will tell you and, if you ask, give you the information you reasonably need to pursue the debt yourself.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.7"><span class="n">2.7</span><div class="t">Fixfy bears its own payment processing costs. They are never deducted from your net amount.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.8"><span class="n">2.8</span><div class="t">In each Platform Booking, Fixfy acts in your name and on your behalf. Fixfy does not buy the Service from you and does not resell it to the Customer. Fixfy does not receive or use the Service itself, and it does not change the nature or the value of your supply to the Customer.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s3"><span class="n">3.</span>Funds Held</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c3.1"><span class="n">3.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy holds Funds Held on your behalf from the time it receives them until payout.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.2"><span class="n">3.2</span><div class="t">For each Platform Booking, Fixfy records the amounts received from the Customer and the dates, any promotion amount Fixfy paid on the Customer's behalf, any refund and the Commission. Fixfy keeps Funds Held readily distinguishable in its records from its own taxable supplies, which are its Commission, the Late-Withdrawal Fee and its Fixfy Client Work.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.3"><span class="n">3.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy keeps Funds Held in a separate account (a dedicated pot of its business bank account) used only for money collected for Partners on Platform Bookings, and records them separately from Fixfy's own money. Funds Held do not earn interest for you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.4"><span class="n">3.4</span><div class="t">Funds Held become due for payout as set out in paragraph A6.4 of Schedule A of the Partner Agreement, and Fixfy pays them on the next payout date.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.5"><span class="n">3.5</span><div class="t">When you ask, Fixfy will give you a statement of the Funds Held for you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.6"><span class="n">3.6</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy promotions.</strong> Where a Customer uses a Fixfy discount or promotion code, Fixfy pays the promotion amount to you as part of the Published Price, on the Customer's behalf, and it forms part of your Funds Held for that Booking. Your price stays the Published Price and your net amount does not change.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s4"><span class="n">4.</span>Receipts and Invoices to Customers in Your Name</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c4.1"><span class="n">4.1</span><div class="t">Invoicing for a Platform Booking is between you and the Customer. You authorise Fixfy to issue, in your name and on your behalf, the Booking confirmation and the receipts, invoices and credit notes for each Platform Booking.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.2"><span class="n">4.2</span><div class="t">Each receipt or invoice shows:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">your legal name and trading name, and your business address;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">your VAT registration number, if you are VAT registered;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">the Customer's name and the property address;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">a unique number and the date of issue;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">the date and a description of the Service;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(f)</span><div class="t">the Published Price for each item;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(g)</span><div class="t">any promotion amount paid by Fixfy on the Customer's behalf, as a separate line;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(h)</span><div class="t">the amount paid by the Customer and any balance due; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(i)</span><div class="t">the statement: “Issued by GETFIXFY LTD, trading as Fixfy, as agent for [your name]. Payment received by Fixfy as [your name]'s payment collection agent.”</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.3"><span class="n">4.3</span><div class="t"><strong>If you are VAT registered</strong>, each invoice also shows the other details a VAT invoice needs, including the rate and amount of VAT included in the Published Price, so that it serves as your VAT invoice to the Customer. You account to HMRC for VAT on the full Published Price, including any promotion amount Fixfy paid on the Customer's behalf.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.4"><span class="n">4.4</span><div class="t"><strong>If you are not VAT registered</strong>, receipts show no VAT and no VAT number, and state that no VAT is charged. Fixfy issues them on the basis of your VAT Status Declaration in Annex 1.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.5"><span class="n">4.5</span><div class="t">Fixfy is responsible for issuing receipts and invoices accurately from the details on your Fixfy account and the Booking. You are responsible for keeping those details accurate, and you remain responsible for the VAT on your supplies.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.6"><span class="n">4.6</span><div class="t">You must not issue your own receipt or invoice to a Customer for a Platform Booking, unless Fixfy agrees in writing, so that the Customer is not invoiced twice.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.7"><span class="n">4.7</span><div class="t">Fixfy keeps a copy of each receipt, invoice and credit note and makes them available to you on the Platform.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.8"><span class="n">4.8</span><div class="t">Fixfy does not issue receipts or invoices in its own name for your Service, because it does not supply the Service.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s5"><span class="n">5.</span>Your VAT Status</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c5.1"><span class="n">5.1</span><div class="t">Before your first Platform Booking under this version, you sign the VAT Status Declaration in Annex 1. Fixfy keeps it as evidence of your VAT status for as long as it keeps the records in section 12.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.2"><span class="n">5.2</span><div class="t">You must tell Fixfy in writing within 14 days if you register for VAT, stop being registered for VAT, change your VAT registration number, change your legal form (for example from sole trader to limited company), or sell or transfer your business or any part of it. You must give the date the change takes effect and sign a new VAT Status Declaration.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.3"><span class="n">5.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy changes the receipts and invoices it issues in your name from the date the change takes effect, as far as it can. If late notice means a receipt shows the wrong VAT status, you are responsible for putting it right with HMRC, and you will indemnify Fixfy against any cost this causes it. Fixfy will issue corrected documents where it can.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.4"><span class="n">5.4</span><div class="t">The Published Price includes any VAT you must charge. It does not increase because you are or become VAT registered.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.5"><span class="n">5.5</span><div class="t">The full Published Price of your Platform Bookings counts towards your turnover for the VAT registration threshold, together with your Partner Fees for Fixfy Client Work and your other business income. You are responsible for monitoring the threshold.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s6"><span class="n">6.</span>Fixfy's VAT Invoices to You</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c6.1"><span class="n">6.1</span><div class="t">In each Platform Booking there are two separate supplies: your supply of the Service to the Customer, for the Published Price; and Fixfy's supply of agency services to you, for the Commission. Fixfy's agency services are standard-rated for VAT. The Late-Withdrawal Fee is also a standard-rated Fixfy charge.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.2"><span class="n">6.2</span><div class="t">For every payout, Fixfy issues you one VAT invoice showing:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">Fixfy's name and address, and its VAT registration number 478 1027 82;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">your name and address;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">a unique sequential number, the date of issue and the tax point;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">the reference and date of each Platform Booking, with its Commission;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">each Late-Withdrawal Fee, with its Booking reference; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(f)</span><div class="t">the total excluding VAT, the VAT rate, the VAT amount and the total including VAT.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.3"><span class="n">6.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy issues this VAT invoice for every payout even though the Commission and fees are deducted from the Funds Held rather than paid by you separately. The full invoicing procedure applies even when only the net amount is paid to you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.4"><span class="n">6.4</span><div class="t">The Commission in the Commission Schedule, the 30% Commission on quoted work and the Late-Withdrawal Fee all include VAT at the standard rate. If you are VAT registered, you may be able to reclaim that VAT under the normal rules.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s7"><span class="n">7.</span>Self-Billing for Fixfy Client Work</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c7.1"><span class="n">7.1</span><div class="t">This section applies only to Fixfy Client Work under Schedule B of the Partner Agreement, where Fixfy is your customer. It does not apply to Platform Bookings.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.2"><span class="n">7.2</span><div class="t"><strong>Agreement to self-bill.</strong> You agree that Fixfy will issue self-billed invoices (“self-bills”) for all supplies you make to Fixfy as Fixfy Client Work, for as long as this section lasts.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.3"><span class="n">7.3</span><div class="t"><strong>Term.</strong> This section starts on the date you accept this Agreement and lasts for 12 months. It then renews for further periods of 12 months unless it ends earlier under section 13. Before each renewal Fixfy reviews your details on file, and it keeps a record of this agreement and each renewal.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.4"><span class="n">7.4</span><div class="t"><strong>Fixfy agrees to:</strong></div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">issue a self-bill for each fortnightly payout period, covering every Booking of Fixfy Client Work you completed and Fixfy approved in that period;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">show on each self-bill: the words “Self-billing invoice”; a unique sequential number; the date of issue and the tax point; Fixfy's name and address and VAT registration number 478 1027 82; your name and address, and your VAT registration number if you are registered; each Booking with its reference, date, property and Partner Fee; any materials reimbursed; any CIS deduction; any other deductions, shown separately; and the total payable;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">where you are VAT registered, show the rate and amount of VAT included, and the statement “The VAT shown is your output tax due to HMRC”;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">send each self-bill to you by email or through the Platform, and keep a copy;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">keep a record of your name, address and, if you are registered, your VAT registration number;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(f)</span><div class="t">make a new self-billing agreement with you if your VAT registration number changes, or if you register or stop being registered for VAT; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(g)</span><div class="t">not issue self-bills after this section has ended.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.5"><span class="n">7.5</span><div class="t"><strong>You agree to:</strong></div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">accept the self-bills Fixfy issues for your supplies of Fixfy Client Work until this section ends;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">not issue your own sales invoices or VAT invoices for Fixfy Client Work covered by this section;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">tell Fixfy immediately, and in any case within 14 days, in writing, if you register for VAT, stop being registered for VAT, change your VAT registration number, change your legal form, or sell or transfer your business or any part of it;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">keep your business name, address, tax details and bank details on your Fixfy account accurate and up to date; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">keep a copy of every self-bill you receive.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.6"><span class="n">7.6</span><div class="t">All Partner Fees and other amounts on a self-bill are inclusive of any VAT due on them.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s8"><span class="n">8.</span>Payout Statements</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c8.1"><span class="n">8.1</span><div class="t">For each payout, Fixfy gives you one Payout Statement with:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t"><strong>Part A, Platform Bookings:</strong> for each Job, its reference and date, the Published Price, any promotion amount Fixfy paid on the Customer's behalf, the amount received from the Customer, the Commission and your net amount;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t"><strong>Part B, Fixfy Client Work:</strong> for each Job, its reference and date, the Partner Fee and any materials reimbursed;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t"><strong>Deductions:</strong> each deduction under section 9, with a description; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">the total paid to you.</div></div><div class="cl l1"><span class="n"></span><div class="t">Each Job is always shown at its full value.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.2"><span class="n">8.2</span><div class="t">With each Payout Statement Fixfy sends its VAT invoice under section 6 and, where there is Fixfy Client Work, a self-bill under section 7. The Payout Statement is a summary. It is not itself a VAT invoice.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s9"><span class="n">9.</span>Deductions and Set-Off</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c9.1"><span class="n">9.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy may deduct from Funds Held and from Partner Fees any amount you owe Fixfy under the Partner Agreement or the Terms of Use, including:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">the Commission and any Late-Withdrawal Fee;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">refunds to Customers where you are at fault, and card payments reversed by a Customer's card issuer, under Schedule A of the Partner Agreement;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">the reasonable cost of remedial work arranged under Schedule A or Schedule B;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">materials charged back and the cost of replacing Keys; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">any CIS deduction under section 10.2.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.2"><span class="n">9.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy takes no Commission on Customer cancellation charges, call-outs or extra materials. They are paid to you in full.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.3"><span class="n">9.3</span><div class="t">Each deduction is shown in the Deductions section of the Payout Statement, and each deduction that is a Fixfy charge is also shown on Fixfy's VAT invoice.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s10"><span class="n">10.</span>Tax Responsibilities and CIS</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c10.1"><span class="n">10.1</span><div class="t">You are responsible for your own income tax, National Insurance, corporation tax and VAT, and for declaring your income to HMRC. Fixfy does not deduct tax from payouts, except under section 10.2.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.2"><span class="n">10.2</span><div class="t">Where a Booking of Fixfy Client Work is a construction operation within the Construction Industry Scheme (“CIS”), such as painting and decorating, repairs or building work, and Fixfy is the contractor, Fixfy will verify you with HMRC before paying and make any deduction HMRC requires, at the rate HMRC confirms. The deduction is shown on the self-bill, and Fixfy will give you a CIS payment and deduction statement for each tax month in which a deduction is made.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.3"><span class="n">10.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy makes no CIS deductions from Platform Bookings, because Fixfy is not the contractor. It passes on the Customer's payment as your agent.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s11"><span class="n">11.</span>Queries and Corrections</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c11.1"><span class="n">11.1</span><div class="t">If you believe a receipt, invoice, self-bill or Payout Statement is wrong, tell Fixfy within 14 days of receiving it, through the Platform or by email to support@getfixfy.com, explaining what is wrong.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.2"><span class="n">11.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy will review the query in good faith. Any agreed correction is made by a credit note, a corrected or supplementary document, or a separate, clearly described line on the next Payout Statement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.3"><span class="n">11.3</span><div class="t">A document you do not query within 14 days is treated as accepted. This does not prevent either party from correcting an obvious error later.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s12"><span class="n">12.</span>Records</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c12.1"><span class="n">12.1</span><div class="t">Each party will keep its copies of receipts, invoices, credit notes, self-bills, Payout Statements, VAT Status Declarations and related records for at least six years.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s13"><span class="n">13.</span>Term and Ending</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c13.1"><span class="n">13.1</span><div class="t">This Agreement starts on the date you accept it and lasts as long as the Partner Agreement, except that section 7 lasts for the term set out in section 7.3.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.2"><span class="n">13.2</span><div class="t">Either party may end section 7 (self-billing) at any time by telling the other in writing, including by email or through the Platform. Section 7 ends automatically when the Partner Agreement ends, or if your VAT registration changes in a way that requires a new self-billing agreement, until a new one is in place. Fixfy will still issue the final self-bill for Bookings completed before it ends. If you continue to supply Fixfy Client Work after section 7 ends, you must issue your own invoices to Fixfy until a new self-billing agreement is in place.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.3"><span class="n">13.3</span><div class="t">When the Partner Agreement ends, Fixfy continues to collect payment for Platform Bookings completed before the end, to hold and pay out Funds Held, to issue receipts and invoices in your name for those Bookings, and to issue its final VAT invoice to you.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.4"><span class="n">13.4</span><div class="t">Sections 3, 5.3, 6, 9, 11 and 12 survive the end of this Agreement for as long as they are needed.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s14"><span class="n">14.</span>Changes and Governing Law</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c14.1"><span class="n">14.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy may change this Agreement by giving you at least 14 days' notice by email, in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, in the same way as the Partner Agreement. A change to section 7 that HMRC rules treat as a new self-billing agreement takes effect only when you accept it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.2"><span class="n">14.2</span><div class="t">This Agreement operates in line with HMRC's guidance on agents (VAT Notice 700, sections 22 and 23) and on self-billing (VAT Notice 700/62), as updated from time to time.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.3"><span class="n">14.3</span><div class="t">This Agreement, and any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with it (including non-contractual disputes or claims), is governed by the law of England and Wales. The courts of England and Wales have exclusive jurisdiction.</div></div><div class="execution"><h2>Signed</h2><p>By signing or accepting in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, the Partner agrees to this Agreement, including the agreement to self-bill in section 7, and confirms that the details on its Fixfy account are correct.</p><div class="sigwrap"><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">Getfixfy Ltd (payment collection agent, and self-biller for Fixfy Client Work)</div><div class="script">Victor Braz de Souza</div><div class="sigcap">Signed by Victor Henrique Braz de Souza, Director</div><div class="sigcap">duly authorised, for and on behalf of Getfixfy Ltd</div></div><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">The Partner (supplier)</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Signature</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Name, duly authorised, for and on behalf of the Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Date</div></div></div><p class="signote">Your acceptance is recorded on the Platform against this version of the Agreement.</p></div><h1 class="schedule" id="annex1">ANNEX 1<span class="accent">VAT STATUS DECLARATION</span></h1><p><strong>To:</strong> GETFIXFY LTD, trading as Fixfy, 124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX (VAT No. 478 1027 82)</p><p><strong>Partner details</strong></p><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">Legal name</span><span class="fv"></span></div><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">Trading name (if different)</span><span class="fv"></span></div><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">Business address</span><span class="fv"></span></div><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">Company number or UTR</span><span class="fv"></span></div><p><strong>VAT status</strong> (tick one)</p><div class="tick"><span class="box">☐</span><div>I declare that the Partner is <strong>not a VAT-registered person</strong>. To the best of the Partner's knowledge, it is not currently required to register for VAT.</div></div><div class="tick"><span class="box">☐</span><div>I declare that the Partner is <strong>registered for VAT</strong>.</div></div><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">VAT registration number</span><span class="fv"></span></div><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">Date of registration</span><span class="fv"></span></div><p><strong>The Partner confirms that:</strong></p><ol class="confirm"><li>the information in this declaration is true and complete;</li><li>it will tell Fixfy in writing within 14 days of any change to its VAT status, including registering for VAT, stopping being registered, changing its VAT registration number, changing its legal form or selling or transferring its business, and will sign a new declaration;</li><li>it understands that Fixfy relies on this declaration to issue receipts and invoices to Customers in the Partner's name for Platform Bookings, and self-bills for Fixfy Client Work; and</li><li>it is responsible for any VAT due on its own supplies.</li></ol><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">Signature</span><span class="fv"></span></div><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">Name</span><span class="fv"></span></div><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">Position (sole trader, partner or director)</span><span class="fv"></span></div><div class="fieldrow"><span class="fl">Date</span><span class="fv"></span></div><p>Signing or accepting this declaration in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform is as binding as signing it by hand. Fixfy keeps it on file for at least six years.</p><footer class="foot"><span>Invoicing and Payment Collection Agreement · Version 2026-10-06</span><span>Getfixfy Ltd, trading as Fixfy · Company No. 15406523 · VAT No. 478 1027 82</span></footer></div></div>$fx$, false
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
  SELECT 1 FROM public.contract_versions WHERE contract_type = 'self_bill_agreement' AND version = '2026-10-06'
);

-- ─── ATIVAÇÃO (só o dono, quando decidir). Uma versão ativa por tipo: ───────
-- desliga a antiga e liga a nova, nesta ordem (índice único parcial da 139).
-- Ativar aqui faz o app pedir a TODOS os parceiros a assinatura das 3 versões
-- novas, e o Anexo 1 (declaração de VAT) vai junto do Invoicing Agreement.
